nistry are the reason the Anarchs have become more organised as of late. It gives the sect much more flavour in my opinion. Hopfully they can keep that up and develop an actual Anarch subculture that feels specific to them and not just &quot;generic anarchists&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also really like the Hecata, but I'll talk more about that when when we come to that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T18:40:10-07:00","id":1463039,"title":"","content":"Just a bump on this thread, hoping to get more updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T19:14:28-07:00","id":1463042,"title":"","content":"I shall eagerly wait for your updates!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T19:23:35-07:00","id":1463043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463039#post1463039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a bump on this thread, hoping to get more updates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, this delay caused by the dual issue of the Sabbat: Black Hand issue and a deadline (that I met) for my latest book.<br /> <br /> I'll get some articles out this week. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T23:51:39-07:00","id":1463198,"title":"","content":"<b>Introduction</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Introduction (Duh)<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A short description of how Kindred society has changed in regards to religion and how populous they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: At the risk of repeating myself, it is a very different time to be a believer in Caine in 2020 than it is to be a believer in, say, 1999, or even 1992. Originally, the handling of religion in the Vampire: The Masquerade setting was that the Camarilla believed Caine was the first vampire and every &quot;proper&quot; vampire was supposed to be able to recite their lineage back to Caine. Presumably, the Tremere got a pass on this because it would be awkward to say, &quot;Tremere&gt;Random Tzimisce we experimented on&gt;Saulot&gt;Enoch&gt;Caine.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it was Revised that introduced the idea that not only was the Camarilla aggressively secular but that it actually was attempting to stamp out the idea of the Book of Nod as well as Cainite mythology. If I recall correctly, it began with Jan Pieterszoon who was apparently using his influence to support the idea of &quot;Kindred evolution.&quot; Also, was almost unique in the fact he was an Elder who considered Noddism to be nonsense.<br /> <br /> Some players and STs, perhaps always uncomfortable with the Biblical overtones of the game, also embraced the idea that the Caine &quot;myth&quot; was just one story among many. Before, only the Followers of Set and Ravnos provided any alternatives to this idea. Either way, both were pretty much treated as being dead wrong. Which is fine, I don't think you have to cater to universalism in your fictional game about undead predators of the night.<br /> <br /> Still, I think they went overboard with the Camarilla's handling of it as we had the woman who printed up the Book of Nod, Ayisha Jocastian, put on the Red List in V20. That would have made my numerous die-hard Noddist PCs very nervous. Still, I get the rationale and makes an interesting contrast to the Black Hand who were always intense Noddist fanatics using that to justify their faith. It also made the Inner Council more EVIL to know explicitly the Antediluvians were real then claim they weren't to make themselves more powerful.<br /> <br /> This book changes not just the Camarilla and Anarchs but also the mood of the game considerably as Blood Cults are no longer purely the province of the Sabbat and Ministry/Followers of Set. While not giving any rules for Paths, they do give differing ethics that takes advantage of the V5 Humanity system and also presents a vast list of cults as well as a revised Hecata. This is cited as a reason the Sabbat are now, well, &quot;EXTRA&quot; if you want a word for it. A lot more extra than they were when they were previously the most extra group in the game. With creepy occult mysticism, Noddism, and fanatical dark religions then the Camarilla and Anarchs now have some of what the Sabbat had exclusively. Well, Sabbat and True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> The book states that only a handful of ANY cult will probably be in a city unless they rule said city like the Lancea Sanctum in Requiem, which is a good bit of data, but these groups all offer interesting new possibilities.<br /> <br /> And NOW WE SHALL DISCUSS THEM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-09-2021, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T01:00:49-07:00","id":1463207,"title":"","content":"<b>The Whys and Way of Worship</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A letter by Aidtya Hay, Ventrue, Former Seneschal of Edinburgh<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I screwed up my order a bit and posted the Justicars' transcript first. It happens. In this case, we have a chapter that is full of nothing but fictional testimonials from various Blood Cults. No point in not handling them each individually. It will be a bunch of short entries that give my impression from the fiction. Here, we have Aditya Hay talk about how he converted to the worship of Mithras and handed the city of Edinburgh over to Roger de Camden. Basically, he comes off as a lunatic discussing all manner of Sabbat-esque rites of mutilation that he is deriving either enlightenment from or simply excitement due to the fact Elders tend to derive no emotion from life save when they torment or satiate their Beasts.<br /> <br /> He does, however, describe something that shows the fundamental appeal of Blood Cults: they provide <i>meaning</i>. If you are a vampire and successfully manage to master nightly survival and even get your own little empire as Elders do then you will find unlife an unhappy dull affair. The only thing you will live for is blood, vengeance, more blood, and petty status among your fellow leaches that you hate. Younger Kindred can feel the same draw. Say what you will about mad religions worshiping 4th generation demigods but at least you feel <i>useful</i>.<br /> <br /> This guy casts out his own childe for not converting at the end, which I also thought was a nice touch. Funny how converts often find themselves a lot more judgemental of the people they used to be like.<br /> <br /> I also give props for the fact that the Seneschal and Ventrue is non-white.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T08:04:01-07:00","id":1463224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1460783#post1460783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the Harbinger's vengeance seems to have been primarily against the Giovanni, I wouldn't be surprised if it was part of a larger gambit. Perhaps the Pisanob were part of the fuel for the ritual that brought about the Family Reunion.<br /> <br /> Another, more cynical, interpretation was the Giovanni offered the Pisanob as a sacrifice to normalize relationships with them only for the Harbingers to &quot;accept&quot; as part of a gambit to get closer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cults actually makes clear the Harbingers are a bloodline of the Cappadocians concerned with assassinations and killing. Apparently the reason they hated the Giovanni is the Giovanni killed Cappadocius and they wanted revenge for the Feast of Folly. AND therefore the Harbingers are not just Cappadocians now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T08:24:40-07:00","id":1463227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463224#post1463224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cults actually makes clear the Harbingers are a bloodline of the Cappadocians concerned with assassinations and killing. Apparently the reason they hated the Giovanni is the Giovanni killed Cappadocius and they wanted revenge for the Feast of Folly. AND therefore the Harbingers are not just Cappadocians now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was always the case the Harbingers were those Cappadocians mutated by centuries in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T09:33:18-07:00","id":1463234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463227#post1463227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was always the case the Harbingers were those Cappadocians mutated by centuries in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under <i>Masks and Murder and Plot</i> and <i>The Habinger Role</i>, Marchesa Liliana and Roger de Camden both explain that the Harbingers were a distinct Cappadocian faction before the Feast of Folly and the embrace of the Giovanni","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T10:45:07-07:00","id":1463240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463227#post1463227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was always the case the Harbingers were those Cappadocians mutated by centuries in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463234#post1463234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under <i>Masks and Murder and Plot</i> and <i>The Habinger Role</i>, Marchesa Liliana and Roger de Camden both explain that the Harbingers were a distinct Cappadocian faction before the Feast of Folly and the embrace of the Giovanni</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://c.tenor.com/cHYRjCIXyckAAAAC/why-not-both-por-que-no-los-dos.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T12:26:52-07:00","id":1463248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463227#post1463227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was always the case the Harbingers were those Cappadocians mutated by centuries in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was, just not directly stated. It was a &quot;mystery&quot; where they come from, but more for the characters than the fanbase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T16:38:39-07:00","id":1463265,"title":"","content":"<b>Time of Thin Blood</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Some Thin Bloods join a cult to try to make themselves true vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: One of the things I liked about Revised was the introduction of the Thin Bloods. The Thin Bloods were what I felt was a &quot;course correction&quot; from Justin Achilli where he noticed that the Caitiff weren't really filling the role that they were meant to in the setting. Yes, they were hated and feared by the Camarilla but not really enough that it felt like a real danger. They also had flexible enough powers that they didn't feel VULNERABLE.<br /> <br /> The Thin Bloods were designed to be manifestly weaker than regular Kindred but more human than the average Cainite. If you wanted to play a &quot;good&quot; vampire then the ones who could feed on animals indefinitely and weren't dead were probably the best. I think V5 went overboard with them and should have kept more of the V20 versions rules but I think they did a decent job highlighting the differences with making them &quot;living&quot; undead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>CT Phipps' House Rules for V5 Thin Bloods</b>: I should note my house rules for V5 Thin Bloods are that I give them the Blush of Life for Free, reduced damage from sunlight, and the ability to drink blood that other Kindred would find rancid (dead blood, animal blood, and so on) but I allow them to be able to get 1 Point of three Disciplines chosen beforehand. They also don't frenzy save for extreme hunger.<br /> <br /> They can use a single rouse check per scene to increase their physical attributes too. Also make one healing per night of damage. Thin Blooded Alchemy is a thing they can get up to 5 points and gets them the option to throw around a lot of other Kindreds disciplines but this is still a rare skill in my setting. They also have to pay for each &quot;recipe&quot; too.<br /> <br /> I feel these Thin Bloods are useful enough to be weaker than &quot;real&quot; Kindred but still have a little bite. No pun intended. </div> </div> </div>What I liked about Revised was that it did make the Camarilla seem more intolerant and &quot;evil&quot; with their Scourges and desire to commit genocide against the Thin Bloods. It also helped inform the Gehenna plotline as the Thin Bloods being slaughtered encouraged them to band together to diablerize or destroy regular kindred. My favorite Malkavian PC was a Gehenna cultist and Noddist scholar who was lovers with Jenna Cross and attempting to help the Thin Bloods in part <i>because</i> they were a sign of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Here the Thin Bloods are not automatically hostile to &quot;real&quot; vampires but struggling for guidance. They want answers the same as much as everyone else and here we see how a cult can take advantage of that like homeless teens and RL cults. Here, they're recruited into the Children of Si that is one of the minor cults that seems related to the OPP concept of the Drowned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-09-2021, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T18:47:53-07:00","id":1463275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463265#post1463265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think V5 went overboard with them and should have kept more of the V20 versions rules but I think they did a decent job highlighting the differences with making them &quot;living&quot; undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously this is one of the few things in V5 that I really liked (well, except for the execution of their Discipline, but I didn't liked many Discipline executions anyway, the concept is good tho).<br /> <br /> I overall liked the rules of Thin Bloods and find them an improvement in V5. I also like the idea of a &quot;floor&quot; where the blood doesn't actually get thinner, so Embraces get harder but won't stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T22:51:42-07:00","id":1463284,"title":"","content":"<b>Brother Sweetwater Speaks</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Brother Sweetwater...speaks.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: Brother Sweetwater basically gives a short speech about how Gehenna is upon the world with the Beckoning, &quot;Swords having been broken&quot;, and &quot;We have failed.&quot; They must &quot;make friendship with their oppressors&quot; and how &quot;only through worship may they be appeased.&quot; It doesn't take a rocket scientist to figure out that Brother Sweetwater is a former member of the Sabbat addressing a similar congregation of them. The sword being referred to is the Sword of Caine and their ideology is to change from attempting to resist the Camarilla and Anarchs to attempting to appease the Methuselah.<br /> <br /> According to OPP's Gentleman Gamer, he said that the Church of Caine's original write-up was basically Sabbat-lite and they were told, &quot;You can't have any Sabbat in this book. Please rewrite it as the Cainite Heresy.&quot; Which I think was a good call and gave us a non-Sabbat bunch of Caine worshipers. However, this feels like fiction leftover from the idea the Church of Caine would be made up of Sabbat or ex-Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of the Sabbat having a bunch of defectors is something that is both extremely hard to imagine given their level of indoctrination and also something extremely interesting as a character concept. That's not even bringing up the difficulties of the Vaulderie. I've certainly played multiple &quot;ex-Sabbat&quot; and have always found them to be great philosophical characters. However, I'm going to make a strange statement that Sabbat defection to the Camarilla and Anarch is actually one of the most consistent themes of the setting.<br /> <br /> The mass defection of Sabbat to their enemies and the resulting changes is ALL OVER V5.<br /> <br /> In addition to the controverisal Lasombra defection, both the Anarchs and Camarilla have both become a lot more Sabbat like. They even mention this in the defense of the SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND tweets. The Camarilla now having its weird occult and ancestor worship angle while the Anarchs are now much more vicious as well as religious themselves. The Sabbat book also confirms that a lot of Anarchs and Camarilla defections DID occut that have influenced both. The Sabbat becoming more radicalized as its moderates all leave to join their enemies and make THEM darker.<br /> <br /> To quote Jason Blood, &quot;Over the centuries, I became more like Etrigan.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Etrigan?&quot;<br /> &quot;Etrigan, too, became more like Etrigan.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've always disliked the monopoly the Sabbat had on Caine worship (have I mentioned that enough yet) so having the option of being Noddists who aren't on Paths or have drunk the Kool-Aid works well for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T10:06:32-07:00","id":1463323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463284#post1463284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Brother Sweetwater Speaks</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Brother Sweetwater...speaks.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: Brother Sweetwater basically gives a short speech about how Gehenna is upon the world with the Beckoning, &quot;Swords having been broken&quot;, and &quot;We have failed.&quot; They must &quot;make friendship with their oppressors&quot; and how &quot;only through worship may they be appeased.&quot; It doesn't take a rocket scientist to figure out that Brother Sweetwater is a former member of the Sabbat addressing a similar congregation of them. The sword being referred to is the Sword of Caine and their ideology is to change from attempting to resist the Camarilla and Anarchs to attempting to appease the Methuselah.<br /> <br /> According to OPP's Gentleman Gamer, he said that the Church of Caine's original write-up was basically Sabbat-lite and they were told, &quot;You can't have any Sabbat in this book. Please rewrite it as the Cainite Heresy.&quot; Which I think was a good call and gave us a non-Sabbat bunch of Caine worshipers. However, this feels like fiction leftover from the idea the Church of Caine would be made up of Sabbat or ex-Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of the Sabbat having a bunch of defectors is something that is both extremely hard to imagine given their level of indoctrination and also something extremely interesting as a character concept. That's not even bringing up the difficulties of the Vaulderie. I've certainly played multiple &quot;ex-Sabbat&quot; and have always found them to be great philosophical characters. However, I'm going to make a strange statement that Sabbat defection to the Camarilla and Anarch is actually one of the most consistent themes of the setting.<br /> <br /> The mass defection of Sabbat to their enemies and the resulting changes is ALL OVER V5.<br /> <br /> In addition to the controverisal Lasombra defection, both the Anarchs and Camarilla have both become a lot more Sabbat like. They even mention this in the defense of the SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND tweets. The Camarilla now having its weird occult and ancestor worship angle while the Anarchs are now much more vicious as well as religious themselves. The Sabbat book also confirms that a lot of Anarchs and Camarilla defections DID occut that have influenced both. The Sabbat becoming more radicalized as its moderates all leave to join their enemies and make THEM darker.<br /> <br /> To quote Jason Blood, &quot;Over the centuries, I became more like Etrigan.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Etrigan?&quot;<br /> &quot;Etrigan, too, became more like Etrigan.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've always disliked the monopoly the Sabbat had on Caine worship (have I mentioned that enough yet) so having the option of being Noddists who aren't on Paths or have drunk the Kool-Aid works well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No no, they were always the Cainite Heresy in the modern nights, but what we changed on Paradox's request was some of the more Sabbat nomenclature, such as titles within the church. This is why our Church of Caine has a more Orthodox Christian hierarchy than a Catholic one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T10:31:33-07:00","id":1463326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463284#post1463284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> In addition to the controverisal Lasombra defection, both the Anarchs and Camarilla have both become a lot more Sabbat like. They even mention this in the defense of the SABBAT: THE BLACK HAND tweets. The Camarilla now having its weird occult and ancestor worship angle while the Anarchs are now much more vicious as well as religious themselves. The Sabbat book also confirms that a lot of Anarchs and Camarilla defections DID occut that have influenced both. The Sabbat becoming more radicalized as its moderates all leave to join their enemies and make THEM darker.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it 100% fails at showing anything from the Sabbat at all, Touchstones and Convictions cannot, in anyway, mimic paths, they fail utterly at it, and the Cults don't...well achieve very little, they are crippled by Loresheets into branding with minimal impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-10-2021, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T11:39:17-07:00","id":1463332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463323#post1463323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No no, they were always the Cainite Heresy in the modern nights, but what we changed on Paradox's request was some of the more Sabbat nomenclature, such as titles within the church. This is why our Church of Caine has a more Orthodox Christian hierarchy than a Catholic one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the correction! I am glad to know the truth!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T15:14:53-07:00","id":1463352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463326#post1463326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well it 100% fails at showing anything from the Sabbat at all, Touchstones and Convictions cannot, in anyway, mimic paths, they fail utterly at it, and the Cults don't...well achieve very little, they are crippled by Loresheets into branding with minimal impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bluntly, you are going to have an issue with my review then because every Blood Cult that lists the tenets of their beliefs are going to get extensive write-ups of how this works well as a substitute for the Paths of Enlightenment and how I'm going to praise it for broadening the Humanity system to include alternate modes of morality. So strap yourself in because that's going to be a thing in this book where I discuss the similarities of Blood Cults and Paths while showing my disdain for the old Heirarchy of Sins over-and-over-and-over again.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I do think this is a good time to mention some House Rules I've been fiddling with for:<br /> <br /> <b>House Rules: How to modify V5 Humanity Rules in CT Phipps' game</b><br /> <br /> * Humanity is not a measure of how good you are. It is a measure of how far you are in control of your Beast.<br /> * The only things that bring low Humanity automatically are diablerie and the Embrace. You need to be a Sabbat to not have that happen.<br /> * Touchstones can be vampires, humans, objects, and places.<br /> * You can be without a Touchstone as they do not relate to Convictions in my rules.<br /> * Touchstones ground you to Humanity and help you recover from Stains.<br /> * Convictions should be at least three things and broad ideas. You get at least three of them in your starting character unrelated to your Touchstones. You may buy more with EXP. The Chronicle also has a Chronicle Tenet that is added to them.<br /> * Convictions help you recover from Willpower even as going against them gives you Stains.<br /> <br /> I may do a complete book about this once I hammer out the details for V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T18:13:23-07:00","id":1463358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463352#post1463352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluntly, you are going to have an issue with my review then because every Blood Cult that lists the tenets of their beliefs are going to get extensive write-ups of how this works well as a substitute for the Paths of Enlightenment and how I'm going to praise it for broadening the Humanity system to include alternate modes of morality. So strap yourself in because that's going to be a thing in this book where I discuss the similarities of Blood Cults and Paths while showing my disdain for the old Heirarchy of Sins over-and-over-and-over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sincerely curious to see it, as I actually agree and want to see your take on it.<br /> <br /> The Paths are an important element in the setting, yes. The Sabbat book had to give rules on them, yes. But this is not the Sabbat book and not the book to present Paths anyway, the Conviction system is an improvement over the old Hierarchy of Sins (the HoS was bashed by fans relentlessly for more than 20 years) and I can't see what's even the point in saying &quot;they are crippled by Loresheet&quot;. Like, what is the problem with the Loresheet rule?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T18:36:25-07:00","id":1463359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463358#post1463358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sincerely curious to see it, as I actually agree and want to see your take on it.<br /> <br /> The Paths are an important element in the setting, yes. The Sabbat book had to give rules on them, yes. But this is not the Sabbat book and not the book to present Paths anyway, the Conviction system is an improvement over the old Hierarchy of Sins (the HoS was bashed by fans relentlessly for more than 20 years) and I can't see what's even the point in saying &quot;they are crippled by Loresheet&quot;. Like, what is the problem with the Loresheet rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely going to get into the ideas behind Mithras and The Church of Set among others that provide different ways of using the V5 Humanity System for very alien, inhuman belief systems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T21:52:17-07:00","id":1463383,"title":"","content":"<b>Protect the Flock</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Some vampires captured by the Second Inquisition get &quot;rescued.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: The Second Inquisition is a kind of threat that works best in terms of being vaguely undefined. Its one of the most controversial parts of V5 because everyone has a different idea of how important humans should be in the setting. For some fans, they should ever be capable of killing all vampires in the world to justify the Masquerade and an existential threat to Kindred. The reason there is a Masquerade. For other fans, the idea of humans being able to threaten Kindred and not be corralled ruins the premise of the game or is simply ridiculous in itself. That's not even getting into the idea of how dangerous or powerful the Second Inquisition should be.<br /> <br /> The thing is that neither group is wrong and the Second Inquisition <i>should</i> be whatever you think it should be for your setting. That isn't always going to work and I find the SI destroying the Mausoleum and Vienna Chantry ridiculous. However, I think that the London purge was something possible and that plenty of Kindred <i>would</i> assist the Hunters by siccing them on their enemies or feeding them information. God knows, my PCs immediately try this despite it being horrific treason against their own kind.<br /> <br /> (My PCs: &quot;HAHAHAHAH *snort* Yeah, because we care about that)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>CT Phipps House Rules for the Second Inquisition</b>: In my games, the Second Inquisition consists of roughly 5,000 permanent members spread around the world that have about 20K people that know a &quot;little&quot; enough to not question why something needs to be blown up, a house needs to burned down, or a guy seems immune to bullets. These include members of other Hunter groups working with other Hunters.The reason the SI hasn't been destroyed is that your average SWAT team member or Special Forces guy is as likely to believe he's hunting aliens or fighting against genetically engineered super-soldiers from the future. &quot;No, that guy has nano-healing! Straight from DARPA.&quot;<br /> <br /> My Second Inquisition also uniformly stacks the deck for their encounters and if someone attacks a vampire at night, it is because they are wannabes or guys impersonating the SI from a vampire's influence. The SI burns down havens during the day, uses car combs, and sniper rifles. They can never threaten Methuselah save through a drone strike and only got lucky with some Elders but are a persistent threat to Ancilla and Neonates. In other words, they are dangerous because they are NOT stupid and do their very best to never voluntarily approach a vampire where they could be endangered, identified, killed, or subverted. </div> </div> </div>This version illustrates that if the SI *does* capture any Kindred that I think that will be the end of the Masquerade for most people because I think of the average Fledgling not having any Garou-esque or even Sabbat-esque loyalty to theri kind. They will spill the beans about the Camarilla, Anarchs, Clans, Caine, Gehenna, and Thin Bloods if they can. They may not know MUCH but they certainly know a little. I also don't think most vampires would hold out on ratting out their fellow Kindred if they know any local hot spots or other vampires. So my view is most Inquisitors are extremely well-informed if they are a &quot;in the know&quot; Hunter versus a pawn they're using.<br /> <br /> This all ties to this story because it shows some wannabe Golconda-types and &quot;innocent&quot; vampires dealing with the Inquisition treating them like monsters. They're actually very dangerous and killed people but that was because the SI antagonized them so it doesn't feel too saccharine. We also find out their cult leader who said she'd &quot;heal&quot; them was lying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-11-2021, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T00:31:26-07:00","id":1463386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463358#post1463358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sincerely curious to see it, as I actually agree and want to see your take on it.<br /> <br /> The Paths are an important element in the setting, yes. The Sabbat book had to give rules on them, yes. But this is not the Sabbat book and not the book to present Paths anyway, the Conviction system is an improvement over the old Hierarchy of Sins (the HoS was bashed by fans relentlessly for more than 20 years) and I can't see what's even the point in saying &quot;they are crippled by Loresheet&quot;. Like, what is the problem with the Loresheet rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree on the Convictions (as presented) vs HoS, but that's a minority so w/e. As to Loresheets: ok say your a Giovanni or Samedi, now you are a Hecata, whether you were involved in the reunion or not, and can pay experience to add downsides to you character to have some of the old bloodline flavor but you can never actually be the bloodline, or your a Lilith cultist, you now have the inverse of your old cult and can pay xp to have some little hints of what was, but you can't buy all of it, you have to pick one or two things of what was a complete package. <br /> <br /> Loresheets feel like a way to scream stay in your preselected lane.<br /> <br /> The Cults fail to be inhuman because they are tied to humans via touchstones, even Shelim is tied to a human, meaning it can never be inhuman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-11-2021, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T00:42:50-07:00","id":1463387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463386#post1463386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cults fail to be inhuman because they are tied to humans via touchstones, even Shelim is tied to a human, meaning it can never be inhuman</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider your point made.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T03:36:56-07:00","id":1463409,"title":"","content":"as a side I tend to downplay clan heceta unity. Mostly the bloodlines/clans in question consider themselves their original clan and the clan name is there to save face . The main de facto aspects of the clan are a series of non-aggression pacts and acknowledgement of the capuchin as clan head. For example while their it's unlikely a Cappadocian elder would pro actively attempt to harm a giovanni neonate it is highly unlikely they'd get any support from them etiher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T03:39:08-07:00","id":1463410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463409#post1463409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as a side I tend to downplay clan heceta unity. Mostly the bloodlines/clans in question consider themselves their original clan and the clan name is there to save face . The main de facto aspects of the clan are a series of non-aggression pacts and acknowledgement of the capuchin as clan head. For example while their it's unlikely a Cappadocian elder would pro actively attempt to harm a giovanni neonate it is highly unlikely they'd get any support from them etiher.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general inclination is that the Harbingers proved to be more reasonable about their revenge than anyone expected due to their (brief) association with the Sabbat. They wanted to kill Augustus Giovanni and everyone involved in their personal genocide.<br /> <br /> Which proved to be easier than expected because the Giovanni have never been a particularly large or powerful clan.<br /> <br /> They've given everyone else a &quot;join us or die&quot; offer and most of the younger family members have signed up willingly. Meet the new boss, slightly less incestuous than the old boss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T03:40:24-07:00","id":1463411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463386#post1463386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loresheets feel like a way to scream stay in your preselected lane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's less a problem with the Loresheets and more with other aspects of the game, like making the Hecata mechanically unified in the first place. I don't think it is a terrific mechanic by itself, but seems pretty fine. It just exists in the middle of other decisions.<br /> <br /> Touchstones I think it is unanimous that they're a bad rule as is? I mean, anyone, anyone at all, disagree? But again, this isn't a problem of this book and I doubt they could add new rules for them. They're part of the more tightly controlled decisions of Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T10:02:31-07:00","id":1463434,"title":"","content":"The Hecata is a sect and about as unified as any other sect. They are blood related, but that binds them closer just as much as it pushes them apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T10:47:55-07:00","id":1463439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463434#post1463434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are blood related</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not and that's the main reason so many people hate them.<br /> <br /> Cappadocians and Giovanni are blood related, but have different weaknesses and discipline spreads. Samedi are unknown. Nagaraja have nothing to do with those lines. They all had different spreads and weaknesses. Now the're all mechanically the same. Why? Was there a reason other than butchering the setting with a non-sense simplification to reduce page count?<br /> <br /> On the sect aspects few people are that angry. It's not a bad development, really, even if not to everyone's taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T11:10:40-07:00","id":1463441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463434#post1463434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hecata is a sect and about as unified as any other sect. They are blood related, but that binds them closer just as much as it pushes them apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not, as others have pointed out, actually all blood related. But they are all death focused, in that for all of the Hecata members death seems to be an &quot;end&quot; rather than a &quot;means.&quot; Which is part of the reason the other clans give them the stink-eyes, which means the Hecata band together. How long that lasts remains to be seen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T11:13:42-07:00","id":1463442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463411#post1463411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's less a problem with the Loresheets and more with other aspects of the game, like making the Hecata mechanically unified in the first place. I don't think it is a terrific mechanic by itself, but seems pretty fine. It just exists in the middle of other decisions.<br /> <br /> Touchstones I think it is unanimous that they're a bad rule as is? I mean, anyone, anyone at all, disagree? But again, this isn't a problem of this book and I doubt they could add new rules for them. They're part of the more tightly controlled decisions of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of them as a great concept but badly implemented. I love the idea that vampires who maintain a human tie are less likely to go crazy and kill people. It'd make a great 5pt Merit in previous editions or maybe a Background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463434#post1463434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hecata is a sect and about as unified as any other sect. They are blood related, but that binds them closer just as much as it pushes them apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I see no reason to have the magic Reunion. Maybe if they made all Bloodlines &quot;offshoots&quot; it would make sense but this seems like an attempt to clean up extra content.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T11:54:28-07:00","id":1463446,"title":"","content":"Well ,when I say &quot;all&quot; I should have said &quot;often&quot; and when I said blood related I was talking about them being literal family. They even call the Hecata a Family of Clans.<br /> As for the Nagaraja they are different and the book even says as such. They weren't called to the Reunion, they just turned up randomly seeking refuge and the rest just shrugged and said since they are also necromancers, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T13:18:24-07:00","id":1463458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463442#post1463442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I see no reason to have the magic Reunion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing the developers wanted a clan as broad as all the others as opposed to an assortment of bloodlines. For people who want a necromancer vampire but don't want to play a generally depraved aristocrat, an elder without a face, a zombie, a flesh-eater or a member of a certain Vodou cult as I recall. Maybe Kiasyd. And some of those were rather small &quot;rare NPC&quot; groups anyway. Hecata are more like Cappadocians with the Giovanni bite (setting further apart mechanically from Nosferatu). I suppose they could have alternatively made the generic Cappadocian community much bigger than previously established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T15:24:43-07:00","id":1463478,"title":"","content":"<b>Planting the Seed</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A Lilin bartender named Joe talks about his religion.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This one is actually one of the more straightforward pieces of fiction and doesn't actually have much for me to say. A Lilin, male this time, talks about how he's set up his blood cult in Portland, Oregon. He is playing a pretty interesting game by getting the Prince and Primogen's permission to hang out in an area populated by the drugs of Kindred society (Thin Bloods, Anarchs, Caitiff, and so on). This, of course, allows him to build up a power base. Which is, of course, why you want to build a cult in Kindred society anyway.<br /> <br /> There's also the usual, &quot;Pain is a teacher&quot; thing of the Lilin that always makes me think of Loviatar in Forgotten Realms and the idea that whoever writes the Lilin is thinking of sadomasochism half the time. Which, hey, whatever floats your undead boat. The gardening motif is also something I am interested in because I do like the Lhiannan from the Dark Ages and vampire plants. Poison Ivy has been a favorite vampire of my Gotham City by Night game.<br /> <br /> I admit, I'm not really a big fan of Lilith mythology in V:TM and feel like she's become a character far exceeding her actual historical value. This is something that the Lilith section of the book will actually delve into where there's a hilarious bit by a researcher that goes, &quot;Why are we worshiping a misogynist boogeyman of dubious origins?&quot; But then again, if we discarded all pop 90s mythology we'd have no V:TM at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:39:07-07:00","id":1463492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463442#post1463442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of them as a great concept but badly implemented. I love the idea that vampires who maintain a human tie are less likely to go crazy and kill people. It'd make a great 5pt Merit in previous editions or maybe a Background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree on that. The whole problem is the implementation, but the core idea of a vampire keeping contact with humanity through living people was a nice touch. And I do think a better rule for it could even had made sense for &quot;inhumane&quot; vampires, as they still define themselves in relation to humans. But it shouldn't be something for everyone and definitely not the same, unnecessarily punishing rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463446#post1463446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well ,when I say &quot;all&quot; I should have said &quot;often&quot; and when I said blood related I was talking about them being literal family. They even call the Hecata a Family of Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still the big problem isn't the lore of the Reunion, but its &quot;magical&quot; effect of eliminating mechanics to make every necromancer work as the same clan. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> said it just seems like cleaning of content, which wasn't something really necessary to begin with and just eliminated interesting options to people who knew of them.<br /> <br /> Writing in such a way that your intention from Doylist perspective becomes too obvious to the reader isn't a good sign, and seriously, they could have just written the Giovanni there and let the others for supplemental materials, as was always done since ever, and no one would complain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T17:14:46-07:00","id":1463503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463478#post1463478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I'm not really a big fan of Lilith mythology in V:TM and feel like she's become a character far exceeding her actual historical value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the cults in\u2026 uh\u2026 <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> are little more than cargo cults. That is they are social structures by people attempting to worship something they do not understand, are not in actual communication with, and which probably does not know about the worshippers. Which means the subjects of worship, assuming they even exist and can be cognizant of the worship, are not obligated to provide anything to worshippers.<br /> <br /> All that to say, the leaders of the cults of Lilith, the Church of Caine, the Nephilim, and so on do not know what the hell they are talking about.<br /> <br /> Exceptions include the Mithras cult and possibly Shalim.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T18:52:07-07:00","id":1463513,"title":"","content":"Regarding the latter, I like the idea of Shalim, the Abyss, Oblivion, etc. being utterly unconcerned with its cult and worshippers (if there's anything there that's truly aware at all), and operating more like a high water table that floods any hole dug deep enough. The cultists just turn themselves into cracks that nothingness can more easily seep through and thus develop powers and rituals unknown to their fellows, but any directives or philosophies are purely their own imaginings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T19:28:20-07:00","id":1463519,"title":"","content":"I'll get to the Shalim write-up later but I actually thought Chicago by Night was interesting for making them NOT a bunch of wannabe pseudo-Nephandi &quot;bwhahahaha OBLIVION&quot; types but people more like Thomas Ligotti or philosophical nihilism.<br /> <br /> Or to use more RPG relevant terms (Planescape): &quot;I assumed the Cult of Shalim was like the Dustmen and about emptying yourself versus the Doomguard and about destroying everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like Blood Gods kind of undermined that by going, &quot;EVILLLLLL.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:20:38-07:00","id":1463531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463492#post1463492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I agree on that. The whole problem is the implementation, but the core idea of a vampire keeping contact with humanity through living people was a nice touch. And I do think a better rule for it could even had made sense for &quot;inhumane&quot; vampires, as they still define themselves in relation to humans. But it shouldn't be something for everyone and definitely not the same, unnecessarily punishing rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still the big problem isn't the lore of the Reunion, but its &quot;magical&quot; effect of eliminating mechanics to make every necromancer work as the same clan. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> said it just seems like cleaning of content, which wasn't something really necessary to begin with and just eliminated interesting options to people who knew of them.<br /> <br /> Writing in such a way that your intention from Doylist perspective becomes too obvious to the reader isn't a good sign, and seriously, they could have just written the Giovanni there and let the others for supplemental materials, as was always done since ever, and no one would complain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book does hint at possible reasons why the banes would have changed, but I understand that some people would have liked keeping all of them different or even just having a choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T22:04:10-07:00","id":1463541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463439#post1463439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not and that's the main reason so many people hate them.<br /> <br /> Cappadocians and Giovanni are blood related, but have different weaknesses and discipline spreads. Samedi are unknown. Nagaraja have nothing to do with those lines. They all had different spreads and weaknesses. Now the're all mechanically the same. Why? Was there a reason other than butchering the setting with a non-sense simplification to reduce page count?<br /> <br /> On the sect aspects few people are that angry. It's not a bad development, really, even if not to everyone's taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nagaraja are , like, 12 people or so: from a metaplot point of view, it's clear that Harbingers brought them into the Hecata fold because of their past TBH connections. <br /> <br /> Other parts of the Hecata Clan are blood-related or were implied to be blood related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T01:18:16-07:00","id":1463554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463541#post1463541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other parts of the Hecata Clan are blood-related or were implied to be blood related.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to the point of unifying their mechanics making any sense. It just took out what made them each interesting on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T01:45:49-07:00","id":1463559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463554#post1463554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to the point of unifying their mechanics making any sense. It just took out what made them each interesting on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IDK, this may be true for the Samedi, for whom the &quot;rotting corpse&quot; image was central to the self-representation of the Clan, but for the other lineages the unification might work just fine. I agree that the streamlining was a bit brutal, but it basically is a retcon, and it doesn't trouble me excessively, let's say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T00:30:04-07:00","id":1463658,"title":"","content":"The gripes I have with the book are that<br /> <br /> 1) There are a lot of different factions/cults in the book, but the informations for each of them are way too little and often too unreliable/unspecific.<br /> <br /> 2) Oblivion is similarly to Blood Sorcery not well designed imo.<br /> <br /> 3) Some story-bites are written like Tumblr fanfiction.<br /> <br /> The thing I like most about the book is the idea that the clan has certain main disciplines, but different groups within the clan have developed the ability to have other main disciplines. I think this would be a good addition to the other clans as well.<br /> <br /> But overall I would rate it higher than every other V5 release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","user":"Ignithas","date":". 10-13-2021, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27028-ignithas","name":"Ignithas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:07:52-07:00","id":1463667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ignithas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463658#post1463658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) Oblivion is similarly to Blood Sorcery not well designed imo.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd recommend re separating the shadow powers into obtenerbration, removing the oblivion stain mechanics and ad some powers from previous editions. A lot of the disciplines are messy and misbalanced in v5 but out oblivion is outright terrible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T02:41:08-07:00","id":1463669,"title":"","content":"<b>Rotten to the Core</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Ken Higashiyama, Brujah member of the Rough Road, a Camarilla biker gang reflects on the changes to the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This one of the stories is decptively useful despite being one of my least favorite. It actually provides something in a way of a sense of how vampire society as a whole is acting to the sudden religious re-awakening among its members. It also is from the perspective of a Brujah that reminds us that while the Camarilla removed the Inner Council seat from the Brujah as well as their Justicar, it otherwise did very little to effect them as a whole. Really, it's not so much the Camarilla kicked them out as a huge chunk of the Clan is in open revolt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla book also indicates that the Brujah didn't lose their position on the Inner Council so much as someone assassinated their member. It is in Screkt's discussion of how everything has utterly gone to Hell on page 120.<br /> <br /> <i>The attack on the Camarilla Inner Circle some years ago was a blip, I believe, and though rumors hold of the Brujah losing their representative (I am shedding no tears since their betrayal) and one of the Nosferatu disappearing somewhere beyond the veil, I feel the city is entirely safe. </i><br /> <br /> In that case, Adana de Sforza wasn't kicked out at all. The Camarilla was just pretending they got rid of her. </div> </div> </div>Basically, the Brujah were going to an Anarch city to slaughter and maim as Camarilla Brujah are wont to do but couldn't because there were no Anarchs. Instead, the city has become a place where many cults were feuding instead. It creeped out the Brujah gang involved and they ultimately left.<br /> <br /> People forget that religion spreads like a wildfire in the right environment and Kindred are no more immune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T07:24:06-07:00","id":1463702,"title":"","content":"Its also worth noting that in the end the Brujah MC is talking to a Ministry Anarch and considers converting or at least finding religion themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T18:07:42-07:00","id":1464668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1463702#post1463702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its also worth noting that in the end the Brujah MC is talking to a Ministry Anarch and considers converting or at least finding religion themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but I took that as sarcastic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T18:08:30-07:00","id":1464669,"title":"","content":"<b>Beauty is the Divine Truth</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A rather lengthy letter explaining Michael the Archangel and the role of beauty among Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: A role of the evolutionary role of beauty and God's design begins this work, which is one of the longer bits of short fiction in the book. This is a suitably artsy and drawn out introduction to the concept of Michael the Fallen Archangel as well as the Nephilim. I've always liked Michael as he's an interesting contrast to Mithras in the fact that the former's claim is clearly insane but the latter is someone who might legitimately be an Embraced god rather than just a Ventrue impersonating one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A commentary on Constantinople, I never actually have used Michael because I actually preferred to substitute Menele as the Patriarch of Constantinople. This is because I did it before the Dark Ages game and I always thought Byzantium made a great place for a Brujah to finally revive Carthage as a dream. </div> </div> </div>I admit, that's part of the fun of Constantinople because it's a parody of the kind of ancients that rule cities like Chicago but not the kind of parody that LA by Night did. Michael is utterly batshit and undoubtedly predates Christiany by several millennia yet has fallen into the delusion of being Michael. However, because he's got Presence 9, PEOPLE BELIEVE HIM and it is able to create a cult that lasts millennia.<br /> <br /> Well after he's dust and nothing due to Mary the Black's efforts.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about the Nephilim is that they're not a remotely deep cult but fit perfectly to Toreador stereotypes. They embrace themselves in all of the beauty, art, sex, and drugs of Toreador like and pretend its enlightenment. I think of them as a somewhat less violent version of the Carthians. I can totally imagine other Toreador getting excessively tired of them too as they put on religious pretensions to just being arrogant elitist Toreador assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-20-2021, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T19:34:07-07:00","id":1464678,"title":"","content":"<b>Bed the Bones</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A Hecate lectures a racist Clan member about proper respect.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This is a funny story but sadly all too true to life where a pair of Hecate discuss one of the ups and downsides of living in the new regime: religious tolerance. Specifically, the fact that one of them has been invited to a gathering of the Samedi around their founder. The Elder also potentially gives her some necrophiliac advice about &quot;bedding the bones&quot; as well as the humorous fact it is the Elder who is surprised that the Neonate actually sleeps in a coffin.<br /> <br /> I also liked the explanation for why some Kindred attend Blood Cults. Not because they believe in them but because they're terrified of the other vampires involved being offended.<br /> <br /> I am getting a bit, &quot;sigh&quot;, about how every scene in the Hecate does need a reference to incest or necrophilia, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T17:48:34-07:00","id":1465455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1464678#post1464678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bed the Bones</b><br /> <br /> I am getting a bit, &quot;sigh&quot;, about how every scene in the Hecate does need a reference to incest or necrophilia, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's especially annoying since I'm fairly sure the original Giovanni clan book only really addressed the incest thing in one paragraph that specifically said it wasn't condoned by the family. Presumably that topic only really came up because of Italian stereotypes. I didn't really mind the mention of it in the opening fiction, the quote right after that in the introductio<span style=\"font-family:arial\">n was unnecessary, but god damn they keep bringing it up. Stuff like this is why V5 got a reputation for being needlessly edgy, bringing up 9/11 at the beginning of the core book or that playtest adventure with the vampire who fed on children.</span><br /> <br /> I like this game despite some missteps and growing pains, but certain writing and narrative choices make it hard sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://for