he-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465462#post1465462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lynch Harkonnen - he's grosser and crazier.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T08:43:04-07:00","id":1465516,"title":"","content":"Honestly I never took that bedding the bones stuff as anything to do with necrophillia. To me it was meant to be similar to how Tzimisce sleep in the soil they were connected to, sleeping on or next to the bones of your ancestors empowers them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:31:52-07:00","id":1465736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465457#post1465457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, it occurred to me today that if I were to describe Augustus Giovanni, I would point to Baron Harkonnen... only less appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always visualized him as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bjH3vNhw1qE\" target=\"_blank\">William Hickey in </a><i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bjH3vNhw1qE\" target=\"_blank\">Prizzi's Honor</a>.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T21:24:05-07:00","id":1465738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465457#post1465457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, it occurred to me today that if I were to describe Augustus Giovanni, I would point to Baron Harkonnen... only less appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oh that whole Augustus diablarizing Cappadocius is just a misunderstanding and an accident. See, Augustus is just really, really fat and needed a lot of blood and before he knew it Cappadocius had drained himself dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T06:45:59-07:00","id":1465762,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay in continuing this but I secured a deal with Podium Audiobooks for a science fiction series, had the release of my latest book (<i>Vampiraz4Life</i>), and also was enjoying being put on sale for my <i>Cthulhu Armageddon</i> book Audible's 2 for 1 deal this Halloween. Business comes first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T06:54:37-07:00","id":1465764,"title":"","content":"<b>Hail Gorgo, Slayer of Men</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A discussion of the legend of Medusa and her cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: The tale of Medusa is one that has often been reinterpreted through a feminist lens. Much like Medea, a woman wronged horribly, the young priestess of Athena got the shit end of the stick in mythology and many people have given their own takes on it. My favorite was BLOOD TIES, the vampire detective series, where Medusa's victimhood is brought front and center but that doesn't stop her from being a serial killer.<br /> <br /> Gorgo's Nest is one of the minor cults established in this book and basically seem to be a Kindred version of the Black Furies with a focus on destroying Kindred who Embrace without permission, Blood Bond, and generally do all those horrible things that Elders do to their childer. It has a somewhat Anarch-esque theme but I doubt many of them would identify as such. The group is explictly &quot;sisters&quot; but doesn't really need them to be female from what I gather.<br /> <br /> It's a believable cult but one that could also very easily fall into self-parody. I am interested in the idea of Medusa being a vampire, though. Nosferatu? Toreador? Otherwise? Gorgo being her childe would make her a 5th generation vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T09:45:35-07:00","id":1465784,"title":"","content":"<b>The Seeker and the Moon</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A Golconda seeker meets with an indigineous blood cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I'm going to be honest that I had a lot of trouble parsing this one because it is the kind of flowery language that a lot of people associate with religious people but is rarely actually employed by them. It is a short description of a vampire's attempt to make contact with a Lima religious sect, however, and has some interesting insights into the Drowned.<br /> <br /> The Drowned are one of those concepts that I felt were left behind by 5th Edition and I suspect are something that will be primarily forwarded by OPP from this point on. They're in some respects a better handled version of the Kuei-Jin. In so much as they are an attempt to do local versions of vampires not related to the Biblical Caine myth and not astoundingly tone deaf/racist.<br /> <br /> I much prefer every vampire to be descended from Cainites because, well, they're vampires and movie monsters are not the place to worry about mythological placement. However, I admit I am not the best perspective for this. I do like that the seeker is fascinated by the concept of them not being descended from the Dark Father, though. You'd think that would make them believe they DON'T have a connection to Golconda them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T10:05:50-07:00","id":1465785,"title":"","content":"<b>On a mission for the goddess</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Two members of the Gorgo discuss new recruitment.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: How do Blood Cults recruit? This transcript is something that provides a lot of insight into the concepts of how Blood Cults operate. After all, vampires are not a huge number of individuals to begin with so they are people who have to search long and hard for people not only interested in being religious but also the religion where you worship, say, Mithras. The fiction lightly touches on the fact that ancestor cults are a bit of a hard sell in the modern nights as well. As one of the two women say, &quot;Yes, she's accepted Gorgo is real. She just believes she's an ancient vampire and not a goddess. That will come in time.&quot;<br /> <br /> And here they murder a vampire to &quot;free&quot; an initiate while also wondering if they're being used. Good Kindred intrigue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:07:28-07:00","id":1465792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465764#post1465764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a believable cult but one that could also very easily fall into self-parody. I am interested in the idea of Medusa being a vampire, though. Nosferatu? Toreador? Otherwise? Gorgo being her childe would make her a 5th generation vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. I wonder how most STs and Players would handle it. How often will it be handled with finesse and how often will it simply become a bad parody? And this is true of most media depiction of cults and fringe groups, and so it will also be true of VtM.<br /> <br /> On a related note, a podcast I listen to frequently is called &quot;Behind the Bastards.&quot; It is fact based and carried off like a black comedy. A recent pair of episodes was about Paul Sch\u00e4fer, a Nazi who once badly injured himself in an attempted to untie his shoes and later ran a religious cult compound in Chile, and helped torture and disappear people for the Augusto Pinochet regime. Sch\u00e4fer was also a pedophile, and as best he could forbade sex between adults in his cult. <br /> <br /> From the outside the cults always look unhinged. From the inside the cult feels sensible - even if the members are telling themselves this as a coping mechanism - while the outside world is wicked and insane.<br /> <br /> Most players are not going to have the patience to run through indoctrination of their PCs. So it may get rushed or hand waved away. Which can tip it all over into parody.<br /> <br /> How do any of you handle depicting cults in a game?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:47:31-07:00","id":1465796,"title":"","content":"I think the interesting thing about how i run vampire cults in my games is that they come in basically two varieties.<br /> <br /> 1:] <b>Not especially noticeable</b>: Blood Cults are full of exploitation, mind-control, murder, and slavery in Kindred society. Which means that the majority of them are completely normal in vampire society. These are basically places to read the Book of Nod, discuss philosophy, and give an excuse to hang out as well as provide a bit more meaning to the existential nightmare that is Kindred existence. The Cult of Mithras, Church of Caine, and even Bahari to an extent tend to fall into this category.<br /> <br /> 2:] <b>The genuinely batshit crazy ones</b>: Just because you're a vampire and the supernatural is real doesn't mean there's not complete nonsense cults here. People who believe in diablerie as a way to become god, conspiracy jargon that vampires are actually aliens from the Zeta Centauri planet, and a pyramid marketing scheme paying of Embracing rich people. These are the focuses of Kindred's lives and usually other Kindred find these guys nuts once they discover just how <i>weird </i>their views are.<br /> <br /> 2# actually are often considered for the Red List and Blood Hunts because even Justicars tend to look at you side-eyed for the basement full of children you drained because it's the way to regain your Humanity through clean living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:17:55-07:00","id":1465802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465792#post1465792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do any of you handle depicting cults in a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>By my part I use to read and study a lot of religions and religious behavior, and documentaries about both mainstream and fringe religions and extreme cults. Ideally with both views from specialists in fields like psychology, anthropology and sociology, and views from members and ex-members.<br /> <br /> My depiction tends to be based on those documentaries and in general on what I know about those people, and I try to be sensible about their relationship with religion, with intense consideration for how each one got to be there, as it does affect a lot of things.<br /> <br /> I'm a psychologist, though, so I don't expect others to have the same type of interest and technical basis, it is just what I like, YMMV. From my players I try to guide them to know what they want out of a cult and play with it, they don't have to be like my NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:47:50-07:00","id":1465808,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, the big benefit and problem of the cults is that they create an alternate hierarchy. Vampire society has very limited social mobility and is heavily stratified - by clan, by generation, by bloodline (as in, who is whose sire). A cult can create a situation where the Prince is below some neonate - nobody in power wants that.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/5e3b268355a25df019c49a616360e90a/tumblr_oc1axhCCYB1r2amcuo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> A different issue are the elder personality cults, such as the cult of Mithras. To be honest, I don't see them being legal in a lot of places. Do you want to have in your domain an organization dedicated to worshipping a rival Prince? No, you don't. Hosting a Cult of Mithras is just a hostile takeover waiting to happen.<br /> <br /> Finally the cults I find to be most benign are the cults for mortals (it's a valid feeding strategy, don't knock the Osirises, and it doesn't threaten vampiric power structures) and in-clan cults. You probably don't know what &quot;Praetorium&quot; is, and even if you do you don't care - you just want the Tremere to do shit for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:55:53-07:00","id":1465810,"title":"","content":"Cults are usually <i>small</i> by comparison to dominant religions and face existential pressures if they draw too much attention to themselves. The dominant religion can be a pedophilia factory and not have it's holy mandate questioned, even retaining the ability to instruct its vast membership on how to vote in elections. A cult with bizarre practices can be subject to negative media attention, criminal investigation and financial audits. <br /> <br /> Like a living organism, a cult can develop a survival strategy that mimics that of an existing animal. A skunk has a pretty effective deterrent against predators. It builds up a reservoir of horrid liquid-stench that it will unload on an attacker so that everything that recognizes its signature white stripe avoids it. Similarly, a cult with gather information about important people in the community, their shameful vices and perversions. When they come under attack, they unload shame on everyone, effectively making a &quot;stink&quot;. <br /> <br /> A cult with Nosferatu and Samedi is perfectly suited to this strategy. Seduce the Mayor with Mask of a Thousand Faces and film the sex with a hidden camera that captures your real appearance. Add some weird fetishes and you have the perfect material for release on the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:59:14-07:00","id":1465812,"title":"","content":"Oddly, a big thing that the Blood Cults represent is that they provide Kindred an <i>international</i> scope they didn't have before. Previously, a Kindred did not have any interaction beyond their city in terms of dealing with other vampires. One of the most interesting random subplots in our game was a Malkavian who was preparing for a months long journey to Jerusalem to meet with a bunch of other Noddists.<br /> <br /> His absence being something that would affect his standing in the city, his ghouls, his resources, and more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:07:26-07:00","id":1465813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465812#post1465812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, a big thing that the Blood Cults represent is that they provide Kindred an <i>international</i> scope they didn't have before. Previously, a Kindred did not have any interaction beyond their city in terms of dealing with other vampires. One of the most interesting random subplots in our game was a Malkavian who was preparing for a months long journey to Jerusalem to meet with a bunch of other Noddists.<br /> <br /> His absence being something that would affect his standing in the city, his ghouls, his resources, and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man. Imagine if there was some sort of philosophical framework that Kindred would be interested in meeting up and discussing. One with notable paragons, famous locations, and important relics. Like what could we call that sort of thing? Something like a &quot;Path of Enlightenment&quot; maybe? Or a &quot;Road&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm being facetious, but Roads should absolutely have been backported to the modern nights after they got invented for Dark Ages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:18:53-07:00","id":1465817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465813#post1465813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm being facetious, but Roads should absolutely have been backported to the modern nights after they got invented for Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, between Chronicle tenets and personal Convictions, most Roads can be ported quite easily to a chronicle in the new rules.<br /> <br /> I agree with the Sabbat's take on Paths being something more complicated, but not all Roads need sufficient deviation from standard Humanity to not work properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:55:00-07:00","id":1465825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465813#post1465813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man. Imagine if there was some sort of philosophical framework that Kindred would be interested in meeting up and discussing. One with notable paragons, famous locations, and important relics. Like what could we call that sort of thing? Something like a &quot;Path of Enlightenment&quot; maybe? Or a &quot;Road&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm being facetious, but Roads should absolutely have been backported to the modern nights after they got invented for Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny how Dark Ages and Modern Nights have such diametrically opposed views on Roads. In DA, Roads are just how Kindred morality is and vary between mortal cultures as much as Kindred.<br /> <br /> In the Modern Nights, Paths are unnatural insane cult-like views and Humanity is innate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:14:22-07:00","id":1465827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465825#post1465825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny how Dark Ages and Modern Nights have such diametrically opposed views on Roads. In DA, Roads are just how Kindred morality is and vary between mortal cultures as much as Kindred.<br /> <br /> In the Modern Nights, Paths are unnatural insane cult-like views and Humanity is innate.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are <i>some</i> aspects of this that make sense.<br /> <br /> First, it's a Doylist design decision to highlight the DA setting. Society is &quot;uglier&quot;, violence is a valid approach to solve problems, many of the philosophical background of our own society does not exist yet or is in the making. You can't deliver on that and the differences between the factions at play if you have to follow standard Humanity.<br /> <br /> Second, it does have <i>some</i> base in reality. Although not every aspect of human morality is as relative as some people think, most are, and we have several moments of changing paradigms in human history, the most recent one being the advent of Humanist philosophy and the Chart of Human Rights. Even most people not actually understanding or agreeing that much with it, those developments had a deep effect on every modern culture, on our religious systems and education, and on our expectations about politics and the state, regardless of agreeing or not with the state.<br /> <br /> But the main reason is simply the design of both as too distinct game lines, which is an editorial decision. And that's it.<br /> <br /> Despite that, as I said in another thread, precisely due to the second point I do think Humanity was the best shot the Camarilla could go after, as it would be the simplest Road for any modern mortal to follow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T20:38:42-07:00","id":1465864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465827#post1465827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite that, as I said in another thread, precisely due to the second point I do think Humanity was the best shot the Camarilla could go after, as it would be the simplest Road for any modern mortal to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I find the idea the Camarilla supported &quot;Humanity&quot; as an official position of the organization to be ridiculous. I can see them cracking down on Blood cults and the things that draw too much attention but I believe that the Camarilla only cares about the Masquerade. They certainly don't care about Kine. If a vampire has a hundred mortals buried in his front lawn, they only care if it's covered up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T02:01:06-07:00","id":1465878,"title":"","content":"My point is - the &quot;international scope&quot; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> described has already existed. Roads in DAV did exactly that - created a cross-clan, cross-nation structures for Kindred to interact peacefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T07:45:59-07:00","id":1465894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465864#post1465864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the Camarilla only cares about the Masquerade. They certainly don't care about Kine. If a vampire has a hundred mortals buried in his front lawn, they only care if it's covered up.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and that's why the Camarilla doesn't care too much about your Humanity rating, as long as you don't enter Wassail.<br /> <br /> But Roads are an important part of a Kindred's existence, up to and including the fact that they ward off Wassail. Well, Wassail IS a risk for the Masquerade. Roads that promote overt behavior too. And the Blush of Life is a nice bonus to keep the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> So the Camarilla doesn't care about the Kine, but can't simply ignore Roads. Of course, there's a reason they don't have the Path Police to crack on anyone not following Humanity, but they must have an official standing about the matter.<br /> <br /> Among Blush of Life, tenets that help secrecy even if not overtly encouraging it, and ease to initiate neonates due to background culture without religious imposition, Humanity is simply the obvious choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T22:58:23-07:00","id":1465973,"title":"","content":"Humorously, two episodes in the most recent casino gave me especially fun Vampire: The Masquerade vibes that relate to this book.<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;The Casino&quot;<br /> <br /> The episode is about the vampires heading to Atlantic City and experiencing a very mediocre vacation. I'm currently reading TRAILS OF BONE AND ASH and the second adventure in that book is heavily based on Atlantic City. The fun is that it takes the exact same take on the player characters being there and how depressing as well as mediocre the place is as a vacation spot. I am only now getting to this supplement and I think you could have a lot of fun with exactly this premise of the player character stuck in an unusual location.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;The Wellness Center&quot;<br /> <br /> This is actually a very good example of a Blood Cult and surprisingly workable within a V:TM game. There's a vampire who has created a cult around the idea of &quot;acting human&quot; (making food you don't eat, listening to music, learning to immitate humans, and doing aerobics) in the belief that this will actually result in you BECOMING human. It's obviously a scam but it actually does make the vampires involve feel a lot better. I'm not sure how they feed but I imagine they're all Baggers or feeding normally and just enjoying the benefits of humanity otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T02:00:25-07:00","id":1465988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1465973#post1465973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. &quot;The Wellness Center&quot;<br /> <br /> This is actually a very good example of a Blood Cult and surprisingly workable within a V:TM game. There's a vampire who has created a cult around the idea of &quot;acting human&quot; (making food you don't eat, listening to music, learning to immitate humans, and doing aerobics) in the belief that this will actually result in you BECOMING human. It's obviously a scam but it actually does make the vampires involve feel a lot better. I'm not sure how they feed but I imagine they're all Baggers or feeding normally and just enjoying the benefits of humanity otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whack<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TsnjbJB.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T03:30:03-07:00","id":1466108,"title":"","content":"<b>Trickle-Up Religion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A short memo about a Cult of Shalim member going missing.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I quite like the Cult of Shalim in <i>Chicago by Night</i> and feel it is a nice contrast to the Nephandi. Rabbi Basaras is a character that I don't think would come off as overtly evil and could philosophically argue the virtues of annihilation as well as meaninglessness. That if you empty yourselves of any needs or wants that you have achieved a kind of inner peace rather than a defamation of the soul. Certainly, something that many Kindred would prefer to being a ravening monster.<br /> <br /> To use a more RPG-biased reference, I always liked the Dustmen from<i> Planescape </i>who were among the least evil factions because they believed they were already dead. Emptying oneself of want and desire made themselves able to live in peace. I don't think the version in <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> goes with this interpretation, though. From what I remember of my initial read through, it seemed to lean heavier on the &quot;Muwahahaha&quot; side versus Thomas Ligotti.<br /> <br /> Here, the fiction just says the cult has offed one of its members and they're being monitored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T03:40:19-07:00","id":1466109,"title":"","content":"<b>Beware False Religions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Someone calls out the general insanity of blood cults.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This fiction opens with the infamous L. Ron Hubbard quote about how to get rich by starting a religion. Scientology being one of those easy targets to take pot shots at but also, honestly, deserving every single one of them. The unnamed author highlights that religions that demand material wealth from their followers are almost certainly scams and this is not a particularly bad observation with the caveat, &quot;enlightenment is a gift from the universe to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also like how the unnamed writer used RL mythology to point out how Mithras the Ventrue is a horrifying bastardization of the Roman/Persian god. This is a bit fourth wall breaking but works in-universe as well. What is less likely to be a Sun God than a vampire? Yet, I could totally believe a vampire takes the name of a deity associated with things utterly unlike himself and get away with it because the miracles of Presence.<br /> <br /> Yet, the idea that Mithras IS the avatar of a god embraced by Ventrue isn't IMPOSSIBLE in the setting.*<br /> <br /> Just very-very unlikely.<br /> <br /> Another thing this memo highlights is the fact that blood cults will make perfect sense to their believers but will almost certainly be PROFOUNDLY STRANGE to anyone outside of them. In a Church of Caine temple, you being an angel makes sense and everyone will nod along. However, explaining Gnosticism and how being an undead horror is a BLESSING is going to strike everyone else as nuts. Which is something to remember with the blood cults. They are <i>not </i>normal and need to be led into slowly.<br /> <br /> Sort of like how the ancient Romans wondered why the Christians were cannibals eating the flesh and blood of their god.<br /> <br /> * I know <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> loves teasing Mithras' sire but I just go with him being the childe of the Antediluvian. What can I say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2021, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T04:00:02-07:00","id":1466110,"title":"","content":"<b>The Lord of the Red Desert</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Fiction<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Two old-school Followers of Set discuss the nature of their religion.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: If I were to list my top five favorite clans in order it would be Malkavians, Tzimisce, Lasombra, Toreador, and Followers of Set with Brujah just being barely edged out because they're so often portrayed as idiots.<br /> <br /> The old school Followers of Set have a lot of charm to them and I think part of that is that they pass the Bester Test. The Bester Test is a rule that I made for writing my genre fiction based on the titular character from Babylon Five. The rule is: &quot;Can the antagonist explain his motives in two or three sentences in a coherent manner?&quot; The Followers of Set were created from the John Milinus Conan movie and yet the Clan Books have managed to take a ridiculous and insane concept: a vampire cult of darkness devoted to corruption as well as evil then somehow make it a coherent ideology. See my above comments on the Cult of Shalim.<br /> <br /> This isn't really a discussion of Setite ideology but does give a pretty nice in-universe perspective of two vampires discussing the Catholic Church's scandals (which drove me from that church), the apocalyptic mood of the times, and incorporation of the &quot;Real&quot; Set's mythology. Mind you, one of the most famous stories about Set and Horus is how the former tried to sodomize the latter but ended up eating semen soaked lettuce but the Egyptians were like that. No one admitted the obelisk IS a penis until, like, 2010.<br /> <br /> *Waring RL mythology and all its dirtiness*: <a href=\"https://wincestuouslove.livejournal.com/34336.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://wincestuouslove.livejournal.com/34336.html</a><br /> <br /> Either way, I like that OPP brought back the classic Egyptian themed wizard Setites. I'll have a lot more commentary on them when we get to the Church of Set.<br /> <br /> Finally - onto the REAL meat of the book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-01-2021, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T09:12:51-07:00","id":1466135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466108#post1466108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rabbi Basaras is a character that I don't think would come off as overtly evil and could philosophically argue the virtues of annihilation as well as meaninglessness. That if you empty yourselves of any needs or wants that you have achieved a kind of inner peace rather than a defamation of the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I have been researching ego death for my NaNoWriMo project. There is a difference in ego death in traditional religions or even Western mystic traditions, and what the Cult of Shalim is after. The Cult of Shalim is surrendering to despair. But then any other form of ego death is probably impossible for vampires.<br /> <br /> Edit: I will not get into religious views of ego death, but in secular views and western mysticism (for example, as it is described by the like of Timothy Leary, Joseph Campbell, and Carl Yung), ego death is an experience you come back from. There is no coming back from what Shalim will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 11-01-2021, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:18:19-07:00","id":1466706,"title":"","content":"Now onto the actual cults!<br /> <br /> <b>The Ashfinders part 1</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Cult<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A Thin Blood cult of rich fame-hungry millennials and Generation Z drug-addicts.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: The Ashfinders are an interesting work to begin COTBG with because they're an unconventional example for Kindred. They're absolutely a cult and very similar to many RL ones. I'm particularly reminded of NXIVM a.k.a &quot;The multi-level marketing sex cult that Allison Mack belonged to.&quot; This an ultra-modern drug cult that markets enlightenment through memes, jargon, motivational speaking, and other bullshit instead of resorting to the apotheosis of the past. It is also a cult that is by and for Thin Bloods a.k.a The Duskborn that has all the sinister edge it could ever need.<br /> <br /> The Thin Bloods are generally considered to be the Diet Coke of evil in <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> and are especially the only vampires that aren't going to be, on some level, evil parasites. They're alive and free(ish) from the worst ravages of the Beast as well as Hunger. That doesn't mean they <i>can't</i> be evil, though. The Cinder Institute shows exactly the sort of rich evil scumbags that would see Thin Bloodedness as a nice compromise with the immortality of the undead but keeping (most) of life's pleasures.<br /> <br /> The short-lived BLADE: THE SERIES was arguably even more influenced by <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> than the trilogy. I heartily recommend picking up the thirteen episode season for some sexy vampires, politics, and melodrama that made a better <i>Kindred the Embraced</i> than it did Blade series. However, one of the things that was interesting about that series was the street drug &quot;Ash&quot; that was made of, you guessed it, vampire ash. In place of drinking vampire blood, junkies could snort this stuff and temporarily gain the powers of the undead. I have to wonder if the creator of the Ashfinders was familiar with this piece of vampire media.<br /> <br /> The Ashfinders are pretty much the embodiment of every Elder's fears about the young because they are going to start murdering &quot;real&quot; vampires to provide their fixes as soon as their supply of Gehenna War ash runs out. I assume they'll also start employing other vampires to Embrace to keep a consistent &quot;product' as well, even if its not going to be the Good StuffTM.<br /> <br /> I like these guys because they're both believable and horrifying enough that their appearance inside a domain could very easily fuck with player perceptions. If they're sympathetic to Thin Bloods, the Ashfinders might be an interesting wake up call. People they like or want to protect starting to hunt them or their vampire friends for a &quot;fix.&quot; The same wealth and power the Camarilla uses now being employed to hunt undead in the name of cannibalism.<br /> <br /> Good stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Fun Fact</b>: The Operator a.k.a Oscar Vasquez from &quot;Children of the Blood&quot; was conceived as a psychopath who found new life in the Blood Bond. He'd never felt love and devotion before, so the Blood Bond was a gift. He was reimagined later as a member of the Ashfinders because the feelings he got from snorting Elder ash were still something more than he'd ever experienced in &quot;normal&quot; life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-04-2021, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:25:24-07:00","id":1466707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466135#post1466135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside, I have been researching ego death for my NaNoWriMo project. There is a difference in ego death in traditional religions or even Western mystic traditions, and what the Cult of Shalim is after. The Cult of Shalim is surrendering to despair. But then any other form of ego death is probably impossible for vampires.<br /> <br /> Edit: I will not get into religious views of ego death, but in secular views and western mysticism (for example, as it is described by the like of Timothy Leary, Joseph Campbell, and Carl Yung), ego death is an experience you come back from. There is no coming back from what Shalim will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting to speculate whether Rabbi Basaras got the Cult of Shalim wrong or the Cult of Shalim presented itself in such a way that attracted him before going deeper into its mysteries of self-annihilation. As a survivor of World War 2 (and a Jew) turned vampire, Basaras is someone seeking an end to the horrors of the Beast and has confused numbness with enlightenment. Emptiness with clarity of purpose. Lack of empathy with lack of attachment.<br /> <br /> I don't advocate the Cult of Shalim but I feel like its just left of actual practices that would be able to lure Kindred in. The idea that there's something that can make you cold to the pain and suffering of the Kindred existence as well as perhaps silence the anger within. If you don't <i>care</i>, the Beast is harder to rouse.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm just reading too much into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:53:09-07:00","id":1466714,"title":"","content":"<b>The Ashfinders part 2</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Convictions<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: The morality of a drug cult<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: One of the things that <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> promised and delivered was the fact that it would present alternative moralities to the traditional humanity system. V5 talked a big game about broadening the Humanity system so it didn't find itself limited to the original Hierarchy of Sins but, for the most part, players were treating it similar to the old one. This struck me as grossly limiting and I wanted the Convictions to be a viable substitute for the Paths.<br /> <br /> That didn't happen.<br /> <br /> However, COTBG comes closest to making it happen as it does provide the cults all with their own alternative moral system that may not be equal to Paths (diablerie will still fuck you up) but can certainly make you be a High Humanity evil bastard. There's no corrections to the Touchstone system either but at least a game effort was made to try to patch things up. Indeed, OPP patches are part of what saved the edition for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>\u2022 Always sample new experiences on offer</b><br /> <br /> The Ashfinders are libertines and new experiences are a part of the package that comes with taking Ashe.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Never withhold Ashe from others who wish to sample it.</b><br /> <br /> Experience and sensation are to be shared. Solitary euphoria is a hollow high.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Never allow someone to silence you</b><br /> <br /> The Cinder Institute requires the spread of its word to draw new adherents and new experiences. Si*lence is a method of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Always listen to those of greater experience.</b><br /> <br /> Wisdom can be gained from those of greater age and experience. One doesn\u2019t have to believe or emulate every word and action, but listening is mandatory.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Always know where your next fix is coming from</b><br /> <br /> Ashe isn\u2019t to be sampled once and forgotten: it\u2019s a way of life. Only a fool takes the drug and fails to take account of their forthcoming supply.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Never allow the kine to realize your undead nature</b> </div> </div> </div>These convictions provide our Ashfinder characters with the morality of a drugged-up psychopath who is primarily motivated by their next fix as well as a glorious sense of entitlement. It is also a morality molded by people who want to spread the cult via word of mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-04-2021, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T18:22:17-07:00","id":1466733,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Ashfinders are easily my favorite of the Cults in the book though plenty of the others are good in their own right. Well favorite after the Hecata but then I've been a long time fan of the Clan of Death so they automatically get my top spot.<br /> <br /> While I do like that the Ashfinders are a cult that's not really a religious cult but a mishmash of the worst aspects of modern cults, the thing I like the most about them is that they actually do something with the Thinbloods that isn't them being utterly pathetic or another sign of Gehenna. With the Ashfinders, they've made them disturbing and monstrous, something that we never really got with the Thinbloods before. The Ashfinders actually feel like they are Children of Caine, bastardized they may be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466714#post1466714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, OPP patches are part of what saved the edition for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're not the only one that's felt that way. I bought V5 when it came out and while I didn't hate everything about it, a number of things didn't sit right with me. And the reception of the Anarch and Cam books didn't improve my outlook on the edition. While the V5 Chicago KS did interest me, I chose to pass it at the time. But I heard good things about it from those who did back and between that and my own love for the Giovanni, I chose to back CotBG while spending a bit extra to get the PDFs of V5 Chicago, Anarchs and Camarilla. OPP did not disappoint though I wish I could have said the same for the Anarch and Cam books. They're not terrible but they're just not that great. Since then I've picked up the rest of their Chicago books and been likewise impressed with them.<br /> <br /> As it currently stands, OPP's work is pretty much the only thing I'm happy about with V5 and if not for them, I probably would have ignored the entire edition.<br /> <br /> Though it will forever frustrate me that you need <b><i>seven</i></b> books to have the full 13 Clans in V5. Aside from the Cam Book controversy, that's easily the single dumbest mistake they made with V5. I get what they were going for with a return to just the Cam Seven but they really should have followed up the Rulebook with a V5 Companion with the other six Clans.<br /> <br /> Then again, given how the Anarch and Cam books turned out, I'm not confident they could have done such a book without screwing up at least some part of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T18:53:16-07:00","id":1466737,"title":"","content":"it's funny, i expected to find this to be the least useful book, so far, but now i seem to be building my entire campaign around it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":27123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","user":"littlewitchmaus","date":". 11-04-2021, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T20:18:38-07:00","id":1466745,"title":"","content":"The Ashfinders strike me as something the S.I. could get involved with, for a game.<br /> <br /> By comparison, the CIA at different points in its history got involved with organized crime, and smuggling cocaine and heroin. I can see the S.I. getting involved with the Ashfinders for the money, for information, and they (the S.I.) does have a supply of vampire ashes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T20:34:49-07:00","id":1466747,"title":"","content":"Random factoid: Peter Thiel is a Thin Blood in my home games. Mostly because he's up during the day and the legends of his weird blood rituals.<br /> <br /> He'd make a perfect Ashfinder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T05:06:56-07:00","id":1466761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466733#post1466733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Ashfinders are easily my favorite of the Cults in the book though plenty of the others are good in their own right. Well favorite after the Hecata but then I've been a long time fan of the Clan of Death so they automatically get my top spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a few more cults I like more than the Ashfinders but they are very well-written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I do like that the Ashfinders are a cult that's not really a religious cult but a mishmash of the worst aspects of modern cults, the thing I like the most about them is that they actually do something with the Thinbloods that isn't them being utterly pathetic or another sign of Gehenna. With the Ashfinders, they've made them disturbing and monstrous, something that we never really got with the Thinbloods before. The Ashfinders actually feel like they are Children of Caine, bastardized they may be. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the big benefit of the Ashfinders are they are able to make the Thin Bloods genuinely terrifying in a way that can't actually be just given to other vampire Clans. The whole idea of vampires being ground down and turned into a street drug is uniquely Duskborn and horrifying in a way that works well for them. It is also a cult that is uniquely modern, Instagram, and feels like something the Duskborn could have come up with alone.<br /> <br /> The fact it ties into the somewhat awkwardly implemented <b>Thin Blood Alchemy</b> also helps matters. The Ashbringers are a bunch of wannabe Breaking Bad chemists behind the scenes after all and might be people spreading it among the Thin Blood population as a whole. I admit, I also find the fact the Duskborn have a Tremere heading all this a bit more plausible than the Duskborn all came up with this on their own.<br /> <br /> It also explains why it's called ALCHEMY unlike a more reasonable chemistry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, you're not the only one that's felt that way. I bought V5 when it came out and while I didn't hate everything about it, a number of things didn't sit right with me. And the reception of the Anarch and Cam books didn't improve my outlook on the edition. While the V5 Chicago KS did interest me, I chose to pass it at the time. But I heard good things about it from those who did back and between that and my own love for the Giovanni, I chose to back CotBG while spending a bit extra to get the PDFs of V5 Chicago, Anarchs and Camarilla. OPP did not disappoint though I wish I could have said the same for the Anarch and Cam books. They're not terrible but they're just not that great. Since then I've picked up the rest of their Chicago books and been likewise impressed with them.<br /> <br /> As it currently stands, OPP's work is pretty much the only thing I'm happy about with V5 and if not for them, I probably would have ignored the entire edition. </div> </div> </div>For me, Chicago holds a special place in my heart. While I bought and enjoyed Beckett's Jyhad Diary, I hadn't really bought back of V20's product line because I had most of my books and the lack of a metaplot wasn't something that interested me. Basically, it was, &quot;I already know who the Clans are so why would I need a book about the Clans?&quot; A very shortsighted view of course. However, Chicago had been where I cut my teeth as a vampire player and I immediately was part of its Kickstarter. I also was uber-excited over Milwaukee and Gary, Indiana being updated for Let the Streets Run Red.<br /> <br /> I was not disappointed by any of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though it will forever frustrate me that you need <b><i>seven</i></b> books to have the full 13 Clans in V5. Aside from the Cam Book controversy, that's easily the single dumbest mistake they made with V5. I get what they were going for with a return to just the Cam Seven but they really should have followed up the Rulebook with a V5 Companion with the other six Clans.<br /> <br /> Then again, given how the Anarch and Cam books turned out, I'm not confident they could have done such a book without screwing up at least some part of it. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the motive behind doing that was both pretty transparent and trading fandom goodwill for sales. I've seen many variants on the same conversation:<br /> <br /> Fan: I hate that the clans are all broken up over multiple books!<br /> <br /> Me: Would you have bought Chicago by Night otherwise?<br /> <br /> Fan: Hell no!<br /> <br /> Which is depressing but hardly something I can complain about it since I just mentioned I didn't buy V20 products unless they were metaplot related.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466737#post1466737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's funny, i expected to find this to be the least useful book, so far, but now i seem to be building my entire campaign around it!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a very useful book and I just used the Ashfinders last night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466745#post1466745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ashfinders strike me as something the S.I. could get involved with, for a game.<br /> <br /> By comparison, the CIA at different points in its history got involved with organized crime, and smuggling cocaine and heroin. I can see the S.I. getting involved with the Ashfinders for the money, for information, and they (the S.I.) does have a supply of vampire ashes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting case of who would be using who. One of the things I like to do with my Second Inquisition is that, unlike the Society of Leopold, generally a lot of the Coalition's agents are subject to human frailties. Bribery, seduction, corruption, and more mundane bias.<br /> <br /> You could easily imagine one of the billionaire Thin Bloods in Silicon Valley turning SI hunters into his own personal blood collectors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-05-2021, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T15:32:27-07:00","id":1466823,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashfinders part 3</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Base<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: The Cinder Institute in Ibiza.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I took some ash in Ibiza,<br /> to show Beckett I was cool.<br /> When I finally left torpor<br /> Felt a hundred years older<br /> But suck it, it was something to do.&quot;</i><br /> - Cover of &quot;I took a pill in Ibiza&quot; by Damien, Baby Chrous<br /> <br /> Ibiza is apparently the headquarters of the Ashfinders and is the perfect location for them to do some recruiting as well as a place to spread their miracle drug. Personally, I find it difficult to believe some Ancient Kindred isn't sleeping there as building a tourist resort over your island haven is exactly the sort of thing someone like the Sybil or Helena might do. On the other hand, maybe they were beckoned and the island was suddenly free for newcomers.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think the Ashfinders probably have much difficulty recruiting Thin Bloods to their cause. While Jenna Cross was building her militant Thin Blood Liberation Front in Revised, there's going to be other people attempting to organize the Duskborn. The Ashfinders offer not only drugs, answers about the Kindred condition, and protection but also potentially money as well as jobs. Security is what most Thin Bloods are going to be looking for and if that means joining an MLM scam as well as dealing drugs then I doubt they have any difficulty recruiting. What do they have to lose really? Their souls? Please.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of one of the (minor) controversies of Bloodlines 2 when it was stated you would start as a Thin Blood then become one of the major Clans later in the game. For some players, it was a complete shock because the idea of <i>players</i> committing <i>sanctioned</i> diablerie was simply not done at their table. Diableire was such a horrifying taboo that the idea you could do it (even though that's what the Blood Hunt MEANS) and not be forever branded a pariah in Kindred society simply didn't register.<br /> <br /> But it also established that for most Thin Bloods, ceasing to be one was a goal. Presumably preventing you from continuing the game as one. The Ashfinders WANT to be Thinbloods. Food may not taste any good anymore but it's not something you violently throw up. Animal blood is unappetizing but it's not like drinking raw sewage. You can stay up during the day even if you're not going to want to open the curtains. Plus, you never have to worry about ripping the throat out of your spouse and child if you get into an argument. I mean, if you're starving, yes, you'll eat them but that isn't a night-to-night danger.<br /> <br /> Respect!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T15:47:25-07:00","id":1466824,"title":"","content":"I actually never thought that becoming a &quot;real&quot; vampire would be a goal for most Thin Bloods. For some, sure, and some more may find that this is the only way to be safe. But to me, most would want to stay Thin Bloods. Less power, better life.<br /> <br /> But I also find t strange that players put so much weight on the idea that diablerie is a taboo. Since 1st ed the books go to great lengths to show you that it is actually a thing to look for and gives STs ways to make it the reward of some stories. Not a temptation, the reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T15:53:27-07:00","id":1466827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466824#post1466824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually never thought that becoming a &quot;real&quot; vampire would be a goal for most Thin Bloods. For some, sure, and some more may find that this is the only way to be safe. But to me, most would want to stay Thin Bloods. Less power, better life.<br /> <br /> But I also find t strange that players put so much weight on the idea that diablerie is a taboo. Since 1st ed the books go to great lengths to show you that it is actually a thing to look for and gives STs ways to make it the reward of some stories. Not a temptation, the reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> I always had the view that diablerie was the great hypocrisy of Kindred society. If you were high generation, you'd try to find a chance to lower it through a sanctioned means.A LOT of Elders are guilty of it in secret or not so secret. They just cover it up and adjust their lineages accordingly as the eb and flow of years means that its not talked about in polite society.<br /> <br /> Its why Blood Hunts actually have volunteers among young Kindred. I mean, no one is going to risk their neck for no reward.<br /> <br /> (It's also why you wouldn't declare a Blood Hunt for a 13th generation versus sending a Sheriff)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-05-2021, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:00:07-07:00","id":1466833,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it strikes me that doing just that and giving a head start to some elder who can barely digest even human blood anymore would be a good way to legitimize their feeding on vampires and get in their good graces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:02:26-07:00","id":1466834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466833#post1466833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it strikes me that doing just that and giving a head start to some elder who can barely digest even human blood anymore would be a good way to legitimize their feeding on vampires and get in their good graces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random Aside: One of the reasons that Elders have been ordering the &quot;destruction&quot; of Thin Bloods is that they've actually been kidnapping them to serve as food for Elder's suffering the Methuselah's Thirst.<br /> <br /> Their blood is a bit watery but satisfies the need without risk of Blood Bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:08:19-07:00","id":1466835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466824#post1466824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually never thought that becoming a &quot;real&quot; vampire would be a goal for most Thin Bloods. For some, sure, and some more may find that this is the only way to be safe. But to me, most would want to stay Thin Bloods. Less power, better life.<br /> <br /> But I also find t strange that players put so much weight on the idea that diablerie is a taboo. Since 1st ed the books go to great lengths to show you that it is actually a thing to look for and gives STs ways to make it the reward of some stories. Not a temptation, the reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on the subject of Thin-Bloods.<br /> <br /> In regards to diablerie, however... I dunno. I'm inclined to believe that vampires are still people, and people are fundamentally good. In the words of Penn: &quot;I'm already doing all the raping and murdering that I want - <i><u><b>which is zero.</b></u></i>&quot; A century-old vampire maybe has enough fuck-ups on their hands where they are completely jaded to the idea of killing someone and do it as easily as they breathe. A young vampire? Who wasn't a sociopath in the mortal life? Probably not.<br /> <br /> Of course, this leads to a divide between being a person and being a player character. As a player, I place virtually no value on the lives of NPCs. They aren't real people, I can kill them without a second thought. I <i>probably</i> won't, but death isn't a real moral dilemma to me in VtM - it's a toy moral dilemma. And as a player, diablerie is pretty much all benefits no downsides to me. Very substantial benefits I can't get otherwise. At the same time, I would expect well-written in-universe characters to have a very different perspective.<br /> <br /> And I think there is a good reason for diablerie (and drinking vitae in general) to be taboo in kindred society. It's the last big step towards the Beast. Kindred do a lot of dancing about to dehumanize humans and make feeding comfortable. Terms like &quot;herd&quot; and &quot;kine&quot; are meaningful. The separation between edible mortals and real people vampires is meaningful. A diablerist does not respect that separation. A diablerist chooses to be a cannibal, and treats &quot;real people&quot; as food. Do you want to be in a room with a cannibal? With someone who doesn't recognize your personhood and sees you as just the next meal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 11-05-2021, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:14:20-07:00","id":1466836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466835#post1466835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you on the subject of Thin-Bloods.<br /> <br /> In regards to diablerie, however... I dunno. I'm inclined to believe that vampires are still people, and people are fundamentally good. In the words of Penn: &quot;I'm already doing all the raping and murdering that I want - <i><u><b>which is zero.</b></u></i>&quot; A century-old vampire maybe has enough fuck-ups on their hands where they are completely jaded to the idea of killing someone and do it as easily as they breathe. A young vampire? Who wasn't a sociopath in the mortal life? Probably not.<br /> <br /> Of course, this leads to a divide between being a person and being a player character. As a player, I place virtually no value on the lives of NPCs. They aren't real people, I can kill them without a second thought. I <i>probably</i> won't, but death isn't a real moral dilemma to me in VtM - it's a toy moral dilemma. And as a player, diablerie is pretty much all benefits no downsides to me. Very substantial benefits I can't get otherwise. At the same time, I would expect well-written in-universe characters to have a very different perspective.<br /> <br /> And I think there is a good reason for diablerie (and drinking vitae in general) to be taboo in kindred society. It's the last big step towards the Beast. Kindred do a lot of dancing about to dehumanize humans and make feeding comfortable. Terms like &quot;herd&quot; and &quot;kine&quot; are meaningful. The separation between edible mortals and real people vampires is meaningful. A diablerist does not respect that separation. A diablerist chooses to be a cannibal, and treats &quot;real people&quot; as food. Do you want to be in a room with a cannibal? With someone who doesn't recognize your personhood and sees you as just the next meal?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of our PCs was a medical doctor who could have been a decent standin for Doctor Douglas Netchurch. He actually suggested the Beast was a biological incentive rather than a divine curse. Without the Beast, vampires would be disinclined to attack humans as their natural prey animal and have reluctance to kill when it is something they have to immunize themselves to.<br /> <br /> As for diablerie, vampires must drink blood to survive and I don't think that the majority of them would see that much difference between feeding from a human and a fellow vampire.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla WANTS to treat humans as a herd and vampires as people but instinctually, vampires consider their fellow undead rivals rather than friends, IMHO. As such, they don't really feel any instinctive revulsion to killing them more than people. As often as not, indeed, I imagine they consider killing fellow vampires better than killing humans if they have Higher Humanity.<br /> <br /> Lower humanity don't give two sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T18:26:08-07:00","id":1466847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466833#post1466833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it strikes me that doing just that and giving a head start to some elder who can barely digest even human blood anymore would be a good way to legitimize their feeding on vampires and get in their good graces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thin Blood hunts aside, it wouldn't work as a strategy.<br /> <br /> A Blood Hunt is for destruction. So it is a single meal. Elders with such level of Hunger need far more than just an eventual Hunt, they need a regular vessel. It wouldn't be worth to give them a Blood Hunt as reward.<br /> <br /> But for high gens and addicts it is another matter. The former want to low their generation, the latter will be happy with any opportunity for a fix. But the former are the most reliable to reward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466835#post1466835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to diablerie, however... I dunno. I'm inclined to believe that vampires are still people, and people are fundamentally good. In the words of Penn: &quot;I'm already doing all the raping and murdering that I want - <i><u><b>which is zero.</b></u></i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you in that regard, but there are caveats. Lots of caveats.<br /> <br /> From the Doylist perspective, what I'm stating is the way the game is designed. If you read carefully, you'll see that the game have built-in situations where the moral quandaries of Diablerie are weakened. Low gen vampires aren't just a bag of goodies, they're frequently <i>a threat</i>. When you are going to kill anyway, because circumstances so require, why don't go the step further?<br /> <br /> The key main tropes where this is thrown more frequently are the Blood Hunt and the torpid Elder. The first is a criminal. As much as a Blood Hunt can be used for political purposes, the game <i>usually</i> makes it clear that it isn't a good idea to abuse it frequently, so most BHs are for real, the target is a monster that fully deserves whats coming, even more than any other Kindred in the city. The second is usually too clearly a monster, and one that will be unstoppable if it ever awakens.<br /> <br /> Of course, it isn't ever without consequences. Marks your aura, may cause crippling addiction, and harms your Humanity. But at the same time none of those are instant game enders. They are themes to be explored, and they wouldn't be so if the game didn't intended for PCs doing it. You can resist the addiction or learn to live with it, find ways to pay for the silence of any Auspex user that gets you, live with a little lower Humanity or buy it back. Those things aren't that hard, they don't remove the sting but pretty much make it something you can live with.<br /> <br /> Under the Watsonian perspective, Kindred society is hypocrite and shows it. Diablerists are talked about in a way that makes it clear that they still exist in polite society and you just don't point fingers without good reason.<br /> <br /> Blood Hunts, especially, are explicitly that. A circumstance under which Diablerie isn't just possible, but sanctioned. If you can pull it, it's your right, as the criminal forfeited their own right to live.<br /> <br /> None of those make Diablerie common, by any means. But it definitely is built to happen in a game, and to be a possible reward for the story, if not from the Prince or something, at least from the Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T19:07:47-07:00","id":1466853,"title":"","content":"While I do kind of get the player taboo of diablerie, I think too many players fixate on that a little too much. I've encountered players so paranoid about it that they think Kindred are actively using Auspex at Elysium and other gathers all the time to check for signs of diablerie or that if you commit it, the entire city will automatically know you did it. And it's not just Cam games either. I played in an Anarch game where one PC diablerized a Sabbat pack leader and another player freaked out at him, declaring that now everybody's gonna want him dead. When the ST pointed out otherwise, they tend got into an argument that lasted far too long.<br /> <br /> Maybe they were in previous games where either the ST was really anal about PCs committing diablerie or had a murderhobo in the coterie obsessed with diablerie to the point it was disrupting the game and the ST punished them, and them getting the idea that you shouldn't be committing diablerie. Or possibly reading a little bit too much into the Cam's anti-diablerie stance while being completely obvious to the hypocrisy of it. Beyond that, I can't think of a reason why so many people think diablerie will cause every non-Sabbat to automatically hate you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T05:36:34-08:00","id":1467043,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashfinders part 4</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Monster<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Beast Shards<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This is going to be a short bit because it's only a very small bit but there's a problem with snorting the human remains of beings cursed by God. No shit, really. Specifically, doing so results in you being haunted by a ghostly phantom that you have to fight and is very hostile to you. The spiritual implications of this are tremendous but the Ashfinders DON'T CARE due to the fact they're not the sort of people who examine the spirituality of their pseudo-diablerie. I think this is a great work for potentially doing a Freddy Krueger series of adventures where Thin Bloods end up murdered around town and it turns out it's due to having snorted a particularly powerful dream-capable elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T06:05:25-08:00","id":1467046,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashfinders part 5</b> (Amber Freeman AKA Thrivehive)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vMv1tt7.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: NPC<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Amber Freeman (Thrivehive) is a horrifying stereotype of an Instagram influencer who has managed to fall her way into becoming a cult leader as well as cannibal.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I like Amber Freeman because she is possibly one of the best uses of Golconda I've had in my game. Which is to say, she's someone who is using it as a buzzword and jargon without any real knowledge of the spiritual elements behind it. Golconda is hard to use in a game as it is a goal to escape playing V:TM but someone who is just grossly distorting it for financial gain. There's a lot of real-life appropriation of Buddhism, Native American practices, and animism for this. Which is interesting because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> is already in the LA by Night thread discussing the cultural appropriation of Chaos Factor.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Amber Freeman is the childe of Naomi Stewart the progressive Ventrue, via a proxy. I suspect Naomi probably thought making Amber a Thin Blood would be less of a burdensome curse. However, the Curse of Caine is not so easily stymied and Amber reacted horribly to becoming a blood drinking monster even if it was the Diet Coke of Damnation. I always like when even well-intentioned sires unwittingly destroy the people they think they're helping as with Arthur Caldwell and Eric Sharpe. Indeed, Amber has ended up under the influence of THE INSIDIOUS DOCTOR MORTIUS (Da duum!) who is a much-much worse Kindred than Naomi Stewart.<br /> <br /> Part of what I like about Amber Freeman is the fact that she's seemingly so wholesome and even thinks she's a hippie granola girl but is actually an absolutely horrifying monster. She's after all manufacturing an empire about snorting the remains of her fellow Kindred and selling enlightenment by the bottle. This reminds me of Love in YOU and Jason Stackhouse's girlfriend in TRUE BLOOD during the first season. Just because they're hippies and progressives doesn't mean that they're not a bunch of psychotically selfish assholes after all. Amber probably has never killed anyone in her life (a rare feat even for a Thin Blood) but she has killed dozens if not hundreds via her network.<br /> <br /> I also love her design. It's very cute and reminds me of STRANGER THINGS.<br /> <br /> The only thing I have a slight issue with is the <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> insistence of referring to the Ashfinders as all Millennials as if that makes them a trendy youth orientated group. I'm a millennial and I'm forty. Amber is 32 as of 2021 and while that's certainly a great deal younger than most Kindred, I honestly think its best to remember they're adult men and women pretending to be teenagers and taking advantage of youth trends. That may be the point as it does fit with the themes of V:TM but I could see some people acting like they really are people in their twenties versus parasiting off it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T07:02:27-08:00","id":1467049,"title":"","content":"I'd like thin-bloods so much if only Alchemy mechanics weren't a complete disaster...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:30:34-08:00","id":1467057,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashfinders part 6</b> (Doctor Mortius)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QKRqCDL.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: NPC<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: The life and times of the MOST DIABOLICAL TREMERE OF THEM ALL.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: The Insidious Doctor Moritus (Da dum!) is not actually the B-movie mad scientist and supervillain that I long portrayed him as in my Milwaukee by Night Chronicles. Indeed, this write-up of the man pretty much states that he is not morbid or weird but I come at my V:TM games from a different place than Matthew Dawkins AKA <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> .<br /> <br /> Part of what I love about V5 is the fact that it has gone back to 1st Edition and revived so many elements that were left by the wayside. Raising Doctor Mortius from being an obscure character in a long-forgotten sourcebook to being the secret hand behind the Ashfinders is the kind of thing that I absolutely love. If I was a member of OPP's staff, I would have attempted to do the same with Maldavis in the Anarchs and Modius as a leader of the Nephilim or Cult of Helena (while bilking them all).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think that Doctor Moritus kind of comes across as a &quot;fix fic&quot; to certain questions regarding Thin Bloods and Alchemy in V5. Thin Blooded Alchemy is one of the more controversial elements of their new status and there's a serious question how the most ignorant and modern of Kindred are able to create such an enormous occult achievement. Even if they just lucked into it, why is it &quot;Alchemy?&quot; That's not a natural choice of a word for people to call their supernatural power. I'd be more inclined to think they'd call it Heisenberg after <i>Breaking Bad</i> or Blood Chemistry.<br /> <br /> Instead, putting Doctor Mortius behind it and maybe starting the ball rolling before his Ashfinder allies spread Thin Blood alchemy via social media is quite believable. I mean, I imagine it would put Doctor Mortius on the Red List (and with GOOD FUCKING REASON) if it was discovered not only that he armed all of the Duskborn with powerful magic but created a cannibal drug cult. However, as far as Doctor Mortius is concerned, it's all about the work. I also like that he is our first identified member of the Anarch Tremere and we get the sense they're not so much righteous revoluties like the Carna claim to be but just don't give a shit about the Ivory Tower or its machinations.<br /> <br /> Which is interesting because Carna is motivated by resentment but wants to stick with the Camarilla because they're still Tremere and manipulators while the Ipsissimus are apolitical but this very stance is a political one when everyone else is choosing sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:43:12-08:00","id":1467059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467049#post1467049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like thin-bloods so much if only Alchemy mechanics weren't a complete disaster...</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the V5 take on Thin Bloods even with the bad Alchemy mechanics. I loved them, and the mechanics just need adjustments.<br /> <br /> Freeman and Mortius do seem very interesting characters and as a source for it. I would make for more possibilities inside the Thin Blood Alchemy, though, bring back some of the mechanics in TotTB and generally make them something like &quot;\u00dcber Inceptors With a Twist&quot;.<br /> <br /> As the blood thins, powers don't get so much less strong as some elders think, but stranger instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:00:25-08:00","id":1467062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467057#post1467057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I think that Doctor Moritus kind of comes across as a &quot;fix fic&quot; to certain questions regarding Thin Bloods and Alchemy in V5. Thin Blooded Alchemy is one of the more controversial elements of their new status and there's a serious question how the most ignorant and modern of Kindred are able to create such an enormous occult achievement. Even if they just lucked into it, why is it &quot;Alchemy?&quot; That's not a natural choice of a word for people to call their supernatural power. I'd be more inclined to think they'd call it Heisenberg after <i>Breaking Bad</i> or Blood Chemistry.<br /> <br /> Instead, putting Doctor Mortius behind it and maybe starting the ball rolling before his Ashfinder allies spread Thin Blood alchemy via social media is quite believable. I mean, I imagine it would put Doctor Mortius on the Red List (and with GOOD FUCKING REASON) if it was discovered not only that he armed all of the Duskborn with powerful magic but created a cannibal drug cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you are getting this, and I'd absolutely hate if this was true. Mortius is not behind the Thin-Blood Alchemy, he's only partially involved in the research of Ashe. He's not even the creator of that - the Thin-Bloods are. Mortius, in true Elder fashion, is a parasite sitting on top of the food chain.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While diablerie is a sure-fire way of becoming notorious among the Damned, <b>these thin-bloods have discovered</b> a way to synthesize necromantic power, thin-blood alchemy, Thaumaturgy, and the ashes of dead Kindred to ingest the shattered elements of the Beast. </div> </div> </div>Making Mortius the creator of TBA would be a god-awful move in multiple ways: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It robs Thin-bloods of any agency as &quot;their&quot; discipline is actually handed down to them by someone else.</li> <li>It centers the Thin-blood narrative on the US, as the thin-blood anywhere else would apparently need contact with this one cult in Chicago to learn alchemy.</li> <li>It makes Mortius the inventor of a discipline he can't even use himself.</li> </ol><br /> And why do you find the term &quot;alchemy&quot; weird? Alchemy as a term is way better known than a ten-year-old TV show. I personally have never even seen Breaking Bad. And given that you are a vampire and thus inherently &quot;occult&quot;, &quot;alchemy&quot; makes perfect sense for distilling magic potions out of your blood. <hr />As an aside, I actually find the Ashefinders to be the strangest and the most setting-breaking cult of them all. Are thin-bloods clueless, dispersed, and disorganized, or do they have a worldwide drug empire controlling major capitals and one of the top tourist destinations in the world? Is the SI tightly controlling electronic communications and travel, or do Ashefinders travel en-masse every few months and openly advertise on the internet? How has Mortius &quot;provided Amber with copious supplies of Ashe&quot; before the creation of the Cinder Institute, if it was the Cinder Institute that discovered Ashe and Amber is the public leader of the Cinder Insitute?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:02:37-08:00","id":1467063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467062#post1467062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure where you are getting this, and I'd absolutely hate if this was true. Mortius is not behind the Thin-Blood Alchemy, he's only partially involved in the research of Ashe. He's not even the creator of that - the Thin-Bloods are. Mortius, in true Elder fashion, is a parasite sitting on top of the food chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but he's still listed as the head of the Cinder Institute and I imagine most of his research is related to the subject and developing it. It doesn't say that he created Thin Blooded Sorcery but it seems a reasonable supposition to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I actually find the Ashefinders to be the strangest and the most setting-breaking cult of them all. Are thin-bloods clueless, dispersed, and disorganized, or do they have a worldwide drug empire controlling major capitals and one of the top tourist destinations in the world? Is the SI tightly controlling electronic communications and travel, or do Ashefinders travel en-masse every few months and openly advertise on the internet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that's not so much a setting violation as literally the point. The Ashfinders are interesting in large part because they're the exception that proves the rule. They're rich, connected, and organized with a lot of potential power to leverage in order to become a force to be reckoned with in Kindred society. Which is exactly the opposite of how 90% of the Thin Bloods live in the setting.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the SI would probably support the Ashfinders once they find out what they're up to. According to the scientific-minded members of the SI, Thin Bloods are still human. If they did a thermal scan of Imbiza, they'd find them all come up as people not Blanks. They might believe there's a connection to vampire society but they will find a lot of contradictory information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How has Mortius &quot;provided Amber with copious supplies of Ashe&quot; before the creation of the Cinder Institute, if it was the Cinder Institute that discovered Ashe and Amber is the public leader of the Cinder Insitute?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's pretty clear that the Cinder Institute was founded by Mortius and he's using Amber as the public face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-07-2021, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:16:56-08:00","id":1467066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467059#post1467059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the V5 take on Thin Bloods even with the bad Alchemy mechanics. I loved them, and the mechanics just need adjustments.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to put it. The way I'd put it would be &quot;needs a complete redesign from the ground up&quot;. Alchemy requires an incredible XP and time investment to learn, huge time investment to use, the distillation difficulties are whack, and as of Cults you are apparently expected to know multiple distillation methods, which makes it even more of an XP sink. On top of that, Calcinatio logistics are completely insane (as you need to keep people in your basement for weeks and months while maintaining the same emotional state, and need to drag them around with you to use the power), Athanor has undefined mechanics (how long does it take to distill? Three turns as per Athanor description, or days/weeks/months as per level description?) and Fixatio is basically fine but level 1 and 2 has no distillation time listed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's pretty clear that the Cinder Institute was founded by Mortius and he's using Amber as the public face.</div> </div> </div> </div>No?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cults of the Blood Gods</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two combined their resources to build the Cinder Institute, all as Mortius provided Amber with copious supplies of Ashe.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:47:27-08:00","id":1467074,"title":"","content":"I mean if Mortius provided her with Ashe in the first place, it seems the prime mover.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:58:07-08:00","id":1467096,"title":"","content":"Ah Dr. Mortius, the man with a backwards 'S' burned onto the side of his face that's still burning for some reason.<br /> <br /> While I generally like the artists OPP has, I've found their artists doing the portraits of their V5 books to be a mixed bag. Some times they're good or great and then some times we have characters in weird poses from weird angles or with weird lighting or shadows that at best are distracting, at worst just bad. The lighting and shadows I can kind of get for some characters to play up the mysteriousness of them but using it on Mortius is weird. He's not really a mysterious cult leader. He's a man of science who's using a cult for his own experiments and studies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for the pair, I rather like the set up between them. Neither really comes across as the dominant partner. Yeah, Mortius is supplying the Ashe but it's Amber that's leading the followers and serving as the public face. And honestly I think long term, Amber's the more dangerous of the two. Mortius could drop the cult if he felt they were of no more value to him and his experiments. Amber on the other hand is presented as more depending on the Ashfinders, fearful of the Cam moving against her and wanting to use the cult as a shield for her. I could see her becoming a really dangerous cult leader down the road.<br /> <br /> Hell I could see her turning on Mortius more than I can see Mortius moving against her.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T13:04:45-08:00","id":1467098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467096#post1467096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell I could see her turning on Mortius more than I can see Mortius moving against her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the fact is that Ashe is going to clearly fuck with its members that they will almost certainly degenerate to insanity at some point. I fully see Amber eventually running out of her supply and noting that MORTIUS is an Elder vampire.<br /> <br /> But Kindred society has that Greek tragedy element after all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T13:52:20-08:00","id":1467108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467074#post1467074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean if Mortius provided her with Ashe in the first place, it seems the prime mover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, again, does not track with the other part of the book. Mortius doesn't control the Ashe supply. Mortius does not own the Ashe supply. Mortius does not have the means to create Ashe. Mortius has not invented Ashe. He trades vampire lore to the Cinder Institute for small quantities of Ashe that he uses to experiment:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the Kindred who mentored the early members of this cult was the Tremere Dr. Mortius (see p. 42), who has been instrumental in providing information and thaumaturgical ability to the Duskborn in exchange for small portions of Ashe \u2014 a drug created from vampire remains \u2014 for his own personal experiments. </div> </div> </div>But again - that chapter is remarkably inconsistent. Being the head of an international drug cartel that controls Ibiza and contains top level thin-blood alchemists apparently warrants only Mawla 2 for Mortius. In the same paragraph Mortius is described as the hidden head of Ashefinders and:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the cult also acts as a group that offers guidance and aid when James needs it, so as their sponsor, he looks out for them and they look out for him. </div> </div> </div>So to me, it makes much more sense that Mortius is merely a patron of Ashefinders benefiting from observing their work, not an actual leader capable of meaningfully controlling them.<br /> <br /> As an aside, for a person with the &quot;Branded by the Camarilla&quot; flaw, Amber's portrait is remarkably un-branded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T14:53:21-08:00","id":1467113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467108#post1467108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, again, does not track with the other part of the book. Mortius doesn't control the Ashe supply. Mortius does not own the Ashe supply. Mortius does not have the means to create Ashe. Mortius has not invented Ashe. He trades vampire lore to the Cinder Institute for small quantities of Ashe that he uses to experiment:</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some contradictory information as you say:<br /> <br /> 1. Page 37<br /> <br /> <i>With the boom of Ashe and the demand for the substance growing, the cult\u2019s Tremere sponsor, Dr. Mortius, considers how best to farm Kindred \u201chumanely\u201d for the drug\u2019s creation. While the potency of the substance is dependent upon the age of the vampire from whom it was synthesized, Mortius has discovered the memories of the vampire can still be transferred over to the drug user and provide the same sense of fleeting joy, no matter the age of the drug\u2019s Kindred of origin. With the Gehenna War ongoing, the amount of raw materials coming in from battlefields has not diminished, as the thin-bloods and Mortius use agents on the front lines to discreetly harvest remains for shipping back to more lucrative market sites. With social media\u2019s tools at hand, the ability to hound a vampire into fleeing their haven is also an option the younger members of the cult have grown to enjoy.</i><br /> <br /> 2. Page 37-38<br /> <br /> <i>Mortius sits at the head of the Cinder Institute, monitoring the results gleaned from Ashe use. He finds that the cultivation of Ashe becomes simpler with time, and the data synthesized from the experiment compounds upon itself. Mortius is in the fortunate position of geting to study thin-blood activity as much as he wishes, being seen as a benevolent godfather by many of the thinbloods,<br /> while acting as the puppetmaster behind an entire cult.</i><br /> <br /> Which seems a lot more important than a 2 Point Malwa as you say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But again - that chapter is remarkably inconsistent. Being the head of an international drug cartel that controls Ibiza and contains top level thin-blood alchemists apparently warrants only Mawla 2 for Mortius. In the same paragraph Mortius is described as the hidden head of Ashefinders and: However, the cult also acts as a group that offers guidance and aid when James needs it, so as their sponsor, he looks out for them and they look out for him.<br /> <br /> So to me, it makes much more sense that Mortius is merely a patron of Ashefinders benefiting from observing their work, not an actual leader capable of meaningfully controlling them.<br /> <br /> As an aside, for a person with the &quot;Branded by the Camarilla&quot; flaw, Amber's portrait is remarkably un-branded. </div> </div> </div>If I were running it and that's what this thread is all about really, sharing ideas, I'd make it so that Doctor Mortius is the Walter White of the organization. Doctor Mortius provided the initial creation of Ashe (with the formula having been passed down to Thin Blood alchemists) and carries out the continued experimentation on it as well as studies. Stuff that makes it able to go farther and last longer while inducing more effects. Amber, by contrast, finds the clients and does all the marketing. No one knows that Doctor Moritus is the science/thaumaturgy behind the cult and would be genuinely surprised to find out there's a &quot;real&quot; Kindred (let alone a Tremere Elder) behind the Duskborn managed cult.<br /> <br /> The Ashfinders could survive without Doctor Mortius as they have already got the formula on how to make Ashe but he's made their existence a lot easier and probably made quite a few of their introductions. I would probably also make the Ashfinders have contacts with the PATH OF THE SUN followers among Thin Bloods. It would be just appropriate that the seemingly New Age and ridiculous cult has already unwittingly jumped down a rabbit hole of evil that provides them with the remains of battle field executions. After all, the Sabbat needs money too.<br /> <br /> Doctor Mortius probably never intended to create an international drug cult but Amber knew what sort of high he'd created when he was using her as a test subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-07-2021, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T17:04:07-08:00","id":1467125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467113#post1467113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which seems a lot more important than a 2 Point Malwa as you say.</div> </div> </div> </div>They control Ibiza or live in Ibiza?<br /> <br /> No matter how international is the organization, that makes a lot of difference.<br /> <br /> It is easier to be an international organization with tendrils everywhere in this day and age. Heck, <b>Onyx Path Publishing</b> is pretty much that, with people from all around the world buying either their PDFs or even the PoD books.<br /> <br /> WoD is internationally acclaimed and every edition got official translations in every corner of the world. Yet, would you say that our community here counts much as political clout anywhere for real?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T17:28:35-08:00","id":1467134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467125#post1467125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They control Ibiza or live in Ibiza?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fascinating conflict really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the centers of power for the Ashfinders exists on the island of Ibiza, where several coteries of vampires dedicated to this cult sample the blood of the thousands of tourists who pass through the clubs, beaches, and bars every year. In a strangely seasonal cycle, the Ashfinders are active in the domain between the months of May and October, but sink into torpor or fly to Portugal, Spain, Tunisia, or Morocco for the other months of the year. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't even aware Thin Bloods could enter torpor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ibiza\u2019s tourist trade drops with the weather, therefore the vampires move in and out too. The cult has no formal hierarchy, hasn\u2019t appointed a Prince or Baron over the island, and has yet to organize hunting territories or Elysia. They\u2019re fiercely territorial over the island\u2019s south coast, where in places like Platja d\u2019en Bossa they receive shipments of Ashe from domains<br /> on either side of the Mediterranean and mix them up with the blood of intoxicated kine to create exciting cocktails. </div> </div> </div>Ibiza has 129,000 inhabitants so it could handle a few Kindred even for an overpopulated domain but Thin Bloods can live off &quot;stale&quot; blood just fine so it could host a much larger population than is typical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite the length of time Ibiza has been a party venue, few vampires took advantage of its throng of drunk, often doped-up mortals until the Cinder Institute set up on the island. Now that they\u2019re there, it\u2019s proving difficult to make room for the Ashfinders during their feeding seasons, which has led to consternation and conflict between them and the Kindred who do make Ibiza a permanent residence. Many suspect a war might be brewing. It\u2019s likely the Ashfinders will seize the island in its entirety in the coming months, acting as an invitation for fledglings wanting to embrace an unlife of thrills and no consequences, and for mercenary Kindred looking to profit from serving Ibiza\u2019s non-Ashfinder vampires in driving the cult off the island </div> </div> </div>In my campaigns before she was put in Indianapolis, I had Eletria as the only Kindred on Ibiza. One Methusaleh controlling the whole island.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T19:55:21-08:00","id":1467148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467134#post1467134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ibiza has 129,000 inhabitants so it could handle a few Kindred even for an overpopulated domain but Thin Bloods can live off &quot;stale&quot; blood just fine so it could host a much larger population than is typical.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a huge tourist venue, Ibiza can host a big number of resident Kindred for its size, and the text evidently make this true. It also puts both groups on the plural.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, I think Mawla 2 isn't so farfetched. It may be the center of an international trade, but this doesn't mean that much anymore today. They live in a tiny domain and don't really control it. They are in a position to try for a big move, but this position is still far from safe.<br /> <br /> In the end, they lack fierce opposition for now, but despite all the money they also lack a strong political pull. How many allies will really come for them if the situations gets hot? What those allies can bring to the island without endangering everyone more than helping? What can they do to keep their local enemies from becoming a huge problem?<br /> <br /> They're bold, and in their corner of the world this may be an advantage. But they don't really have the resources to withstand a protracted battle against a serious threat, their biggest advantage is the lack of such serious threat. If things heat up, I'd say they will need to move quickly to have a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:56:26-08:00","id":1467177,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashfinders part 7</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Rituals<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: What the Ashfinders have come up with.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: The final part of the Ashfinders is a short list of abilities that Ashe can provide and what sort of abilities you need with Thin Blood Alchemy to create Ashe. The cult doesn't really break the mold with these abilities and I'm pretty much of the mind that its abilities are not that different from what Thin Blooded Alchemy should be able to come up with normally.<br /> <br /> This is going to be a somewhat controversial opinion but I thin Thin Blooded Alchemy was a poor decision on the part of the writers to try to make Thin Bloods more viable gameplay wise. Personally, I think it'd have been better if they'd stuck with the idea that Thin Bloods can either get up to 3 in Disciplines and no higher or 1 dot in any Discipline with the possibility of having their own personal Discipline. If you're going to play Thin Bloods then you're wanting to avoid power gaming in the first place.<br /> <br /> Maybe also make them able to take Numina like True Faith or Hedge Magic. As such, this tells you how they can make Ashe and also replicate other Kindred's disciplines that they have literally smoked.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:58:41-08:00","id":1467180,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashfinders part 8</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Conclusion<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: These guys are fucked.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: Overall, the Ashfinders are an excellent cult and a group that can definitely add an element of horror to the Thin Bloods. They're adapting to become the same kind of vicious evil monsters as other Kindred and the cannibalism element plays into the very same stereotypes that the Elders have had about the Duskborn.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Ashfinders are long for the world, though. This is an organization that once its particular drug of choice dries out is going to have a very nasty crash. Unlike Elder Blood, Elder ashe is a non-renewable resource and the Gehenna War is eventually going to peter out in terms of supply. They might be able to Embrace younger Kindred for a &quot;weak&quot; version of Ashe but that's not going to be too great of a supply and will cause their Humanity to plummet like a stone.<br /> <br /> I predict the Ashfinders are eventually going to receive a meeting from a Justicar in Ibiza and they are going to exterminate the cult root to stem. I also wouldn't be surprised if Mortius did end up on the Red List for his role in creating such an organization. As mentioned, the Ashfiners pretty much play into a trifecta of Elder fears: diablerie, Thin Bloods, and modern technology that endangers the Masquerade. It will probably spill over and get Naomi Stewart destroyed as well unless she's the person who decides to destroy the Thin Bloods (and lose Humanity in the process). I suspect Ashe the formula will survive the destruction of the Ashfinders but something used much-much more judiciously as a weapon by Thin Bloods rather than a party drug.<br /> <br /> That's also the BEST outcome for these people since I could easily also see the Ashfinders suffering a more supernatural PSA ending where their rampant use of smoking Elders results in them becoming the first Thin Bloods to become wights as the Beast Shards destroy them and leave them a bunch of drugged out murderous monsters possessed by the fragments of the Damned. You could even go full Poltergeist and have the Cindy Incident sucked into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-08-2021, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T12:49:01-08:00","id":1467192,"title":"","content":"I still think it is possible (for an interesting campaign) for the S.I. to take over the Ashfinders operation. Also, if a gaming group is willing to get into deep body horror territory, the Ashfinders might stake some elder - such as Mortis himself - and cut off the elder's arms and legs and make ashe from the limbs, wait for the elder to regrow the limbs and do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T14:53:29-08:00","id":1467199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467177#post1467177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to be a somewhat controversial opinion but I thin Thin Blooded Alchemy was a poor decision on the part of the writers to try to make Thin Bloods more viable gameplay wise. Personally, I think it'd have been better if they'd stuck with the idea that Thin Bloods can either get up to 3 in Disciplines and no higher or 1 dot in any Discipline with the possibility of having their own personal Discipline. If you're going to play Thin Bloods then you're wanting to avoid power gaming in the first place.<br /> <br /> Maybe also make them able to take Numina like True Faith or Hedge Magic. As such, this tells you how they can make Ashe and also replicate other Kindred's disciplines that they have literally smoked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed I, at least, disagree, although I can understand the concern. And I do think that access to Numina would be a very interesting twist for them to work with.<br /> <br /> 1 - As an ST I like a sense of balance because it actually makes my work easier when exploring different chronicle styles. With mechanical balance I can have a mixed group without players feeling cheated, and I can have a &quot;low level&quot; chronicle without robbing myself of the option of high challenges for the players at a later moment;<br /> <br /> <u><i>Corollary:</i></u> Balance doesn't mean perfect math or anything like that. What it means is that players feel like all the options are valid and interesting, and that any drawback is worth the advantages <i>for the player</i>. A character don't have to feel the same, but the old saying that choosing a weaker option just for the challenge makes you a better player is BS.<br /> <br /> 2 - More importantly, I like the concept for both Caitiff and Thin Blood that those vampires have <i>stranger</i> powers, regardless of strength. That those weird vampires play by other rules no one is sure about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467180#post1467180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Type</b>: Conclusion<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: These guys are fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly agree, but I can see their storyline going some other ways.<br /> <br /> As much as their supply is doomed to diminish greatly, it doesn't mean they will be without something to offer, especially with Mortius still studying Ashe and other things. They may learn how to sacrifice quality for quantity, to get more from a lesser supply. They may develop a way to extract it from living Elders as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> describes. They may even learn how to extract Ashe from previous Ashe users, encouraging addiction to make the future supply.<br /> <br /> They may also learn the secrets of other drugs and stuff that fit their theme. So one day they stop churning out Ashe, but start to deliver other things.<br /> <br /> I totally agree, though, that they'll be on a Justicar's to do list ASAP if they just stay as they are. But their first real clashes with Kindred power may also make them learn to adapt and find a niche. They don't need to be influential in the Camarilla, just to have enough clout to stay in peace at their little corner of the world.<br /> <br /> One of the things that makes such small scale organizations operate all around the world is that, actually, their supply chains are their own thing. They certainly encourage the destruction of elders for production of Ashe, but they're also less murderers and more receptors. Bigger Jyhad players may start to use those chains and use the cult as a dump for their own purposes, and keep them under protection.<br /> <br /> What if Ashe becomes an alternative for Diablerie's high, for example? A number of elders are addicted to Diablerie, and they may decide that the marvelous dust makes their lives easier and better and they don't need to know where it comes from, or not care even if they know. It may make human, or even animal, blood work and taste as elder vitae, turning their product into a highly sought after asset.<br /> <br /> Finally, they may end up getting SI protection instead, making Ibiza into the definitive Elder Hell: a seat of power and money in the hands of Thin Blood and protected by cutting edge technology in the hands of humans that already know too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T17:27:59-08:00","id":1467209,"title":"","content":"With regards to the Thin-bloods, I've long had a mixed opinion on them, stretching back to the Rev Ed days. I don't hate Thin-blood Alchemy and in theory, like it as a concept (I haven't played V5 much less as a Thin-blood or with one so I can't attest to how it plays) but I do find it questionable as the sole Discipline of the Thin-bloods. An opinion? Sure. But the sole Discipline? That I struggle with.<br /> <br /> But honestly that's kind of the problem with Thin-bloods. They're supposed to be a watered down version of Kindred but if you make them too weak, why play them? And to be frank, I've never been in game with a Thin-blood PC. None of the people I've gamed with ever expressed an interest in playing them. And I can kind of get why. They're looked down upon by many in-universe and quiet weak. There's really not much of reason to play them, especially when we have long had Caitiff and Ghouls.<br /> <br /> So I can get why they would give them Thin-blood Alchemy as something new and cool to get people interested in playing them. But limiting them to what is basically Blood Sorcery: Gutter Magick Edition was a wrong move. Blood Sorcery has to be taught from another or created through experimentation which wouldn't be a viable thing for every Thin-blood character but now that's all they have. And in the case of the latter, it would still require the Thin-blood to think of experimenting with blood, theirs and that of mortals. So yeah, if the Thin-blood doesn't have connections with other Thin-bloods or a curiosity towards their new condition, where exactly would they pick up the knowledge of Alchemy?<br /> <br /> Thin-blood Alchemy is an interesting concept but with a flawed execution.<br /> <br /> As for CTPhipps' final thoughts on the Ashfinders, I pretty much agree. Long term, the odds are not good for them surviving. Not completely impossible but not good either. The real question will be how effective the Cam will be once they eventually hit them. I could see them being less than successful in destroying the Ashfinders, getting most or all the people at the top but the cult as a whole fragmenting, leading to several successor cults that spread the ideas of the cult and Ashe further across the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T18:19:34-08:00","id":1467212,"title":"","content":"I have played with a couple of thin-bloods, and from what I gather, being generally weaker is part of the appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T18:28:45-08:00","id":1467213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467212#post1467212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have played with a couple of thin-bloods, and from what I gather, being generally weaker is part of the appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah, which means amping up their power is a problem.<br /> <br /> You play a Thin Blood for RP reasons.<br /> <br /> Same as playing a Hunter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T20:21:36-08:00","id":1467230,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I haven't thought about the RP appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T04:43:00-08:00","id":1467250,"title":"","content":"I don't personally think it fair outside an All Thin Bloods game. As much as some players do like to make such choices I was always irked by this argument when you have a character concept that could work in a mixed group, but is avoided because it is an objectively worse option without needing to be.<br /> <br /> Of course, my experience also includes a lot of pedantic players that like to defend that such differences make for a superior RP challenge and players that complain are just &quot;inferior roleplayers that should grow up or go back to their D&amp;D and video games&quot;. That was the particular brand of derision I found the most among WoD's bullies.<br /> <br /> But mechanical balance don't have to mess with the notion of being weaker or less potent from a Watsonian perspective. What it must do is give <i>something</i> for the <b><u>player's</u></b> troubles. A hard limit of 3 dots, but less XP cost for learning Disciplines would be an example, although not my favorite route either.<br /> <br /> As I said, I like the notion of the Thin Blood having weirder powers than the other Kindred. While Caitiff may create new Disciplines with ease, the Thin Bloods having an easy time spontaneously developing Numina would be a nice touch, or maybe having Disciplines dots that get reallocated at random every number of nights. One could have a number of dots in Discipline that wax and wane with the moon.<br /> <br /> Thin Bloods already have several weaknesses outside messing with the Disciplines. I like 'em weirder to compensate, not just overall weaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T15:22:31-08:00","id":1467295,"title":"","content":"An interesting, if practically so-so ability of thin-bloods, is how they get a dot of a discipline based on the resonance of their last meal, two if it's Intense. So by choosing their blood carefully, they can swap discipline at will. I don't know that means they can choose their particular discipline power, but then I don't see how that works for potent vampires either. I see thin-blood alchemy as a refinement of this practice, which involves creating new resonances that confer powers to which other vampires lack natural access, because their vitae isn't flexible enough. Although perhaps it would be possible on a regular diet of given formula.<br /> <br /> All V5 kindred respond to resonance, but for thin-bloods, one of the effects is instant, tangible and reliable. I think what they lack is heriditary resonance and the ability to <i>cumulatively</i> develop their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T18:49:12-08:00","id":1467966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1466747#post1466747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random factoid: Peter Thiel is a Thin Blood in my home games. Mostly because he's up during the day and the legends of his weird blood rituals.<br /> <br /> He'd make a perfect Ashfinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>... You mad genius, I so want to use that in a chronicle. Peter Thiel investing in Parabiosis was part of some weird Thin-Blood alchemy experiment or an attempt to give his mortal cover an excuse as to why he's always around blood.<br /> <br /> Now I either have to research Peter Thiel's life to figure out if I can justify him showing up already embraced and funding Parabiosis research when my chronicle's set in 1992, or I have to wait for the timeline to advance to the point it makes sense for him to show up...<br /> <br /> To comment on the meat of this discussion; I originally didn't think much of the Ashfinders, just some weird group of druggies snorting vampire ash. But all the details of how their organization came to be and how they operate really raised my opinion after I got my copy of <i>Cults. </i>The Beast Shards alone adds so much potential for stories, and there's still more you can dig into. I mean with a large group of social media influencers in on the Masquerade, the thought of a bunch of Duskborn <i>doxxing </i>an elder into submission and then killing them and turning their remains into drugs. That's the crazy messed up stuff I like in my WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13528-lordpyrus25","name":"LordPyrus25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T07:34:41-08:00","id":1468269,"title":"","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I haven't been updating this thread was due to the fact that I am currently working on doing my TRAILS OF ASH AND BONE campaign preparation work. I already did THE SACRIFICE, THE FALL OF LONDON, and LET THE STREETS RUN RED campaigns with these characters but am now working to adapt this one.<br /> <br /> One big change I'm making is that the adventures will all take place in one area rather than split across multiple parts of the world. Specifically, I'm going to be having the adventures take place in the Florida and Cuba area. This is a pretty big change but it'll allow the adventures to be tied together easier. Another change is that in addition to the focus on the Hecata, I'm going to add a subplot about the player characters trying to set up a blood trade as well as dealing with the Ashfinders as well as Circulatory system.<br /> <br /> Should be fun even if I'm going to have to create a Hecate mastermind to tie it all together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T08:09:30-08:00","id":1468271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1468269#post1468269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, I'm going to be having the adventures take place in the Florida and Cuba area.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offence and not that it's any of my business, but I already dislike your adaptation of <i>Old Wounds</i>:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is Tampa. We are at our most serious when joking, our most deadly when at play. Our smile is our snarl. Our laughter is our battle cry. We move sideways, ever sideways, like monstrous crabs.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T09:03:25-08:00","id":1468277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1468271#post1468271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offence and not that it's any of my business, but I already dislike your adaptation of <i>Old Wounds</i>:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is Tampa. We are at our most serious when joking, our most deadly when at play. Our smile is our snarl. Our laughter is our battle cry. We move sideways, ever sideways, like monstrous crabs.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why it should be Cuba for that part.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, my games ARE normally set in Tampa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T05:58:04-08:00","id":1473067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467043#post1467043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ashfinders part 4</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Monster<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: Beast Shards<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: This is going to be a short bit because it's only a very small bit but there's a problem with snorting the human remains of beings cursed by God. No shit, really. Specifically, doing so results in you being haunted by a ghostly phantom that you have to fight and is very hostile to you. The spiritual implications of this are tremendous but the Ashfinders DON'T CARE due to the fact they're not the sort of people who examine the spirituality of their pseudo-diablerie. I think this is a great work for potentially doing a Freddy Krueger series of adventures where Thin Bloods end up murdered around town and it turns out it's due to having snorted a particularly powerful dream-capable elder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, have done something like this as an alternate weakness for Caitiff. Not exactly an elder, but every Caitiff is haunted by the shade of a destroyed vampire its sire consumed or had a blood bond with around the time of the Caitiff's embrace.<br /> <br /> As an aside, now considering how i might or not spin Mortius' connection to the Ashfinders into the already existent subplots of my BJD-influenced &quot;Milwaukee under siege&quot; game...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordPyrus25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1467966#post1467966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... You mad genius, I so want to use that in a chronicle. Peter Thiel investing in Parabiosis was part of some weird Thin-Blood alchemy experiment or an attempt to give his mortal cover an excuse as to why he's always around blood.<br /> <br /> Now I either have to research Peter Thiel's life to figure out if I can justify him showing up already embraced and funding Parabiosis research when my chronicle's set in 1992, or I have to wait for the timeline to advance to the point it makes sense for him to show up...<br /> <br /> To comment on the meat of this discussion; I originally didn't think much of the Ashfinders, just some weird group of druggies snorting vampire ash. But all the details of how their organization came to be and how they operate really raised my opinion after I got my copy of <i>Cults. </i>The Beast Shards alone adds so much potential for stories, and there's still more you can dig into. I mean with a large group of social media influencers in on the Masquerade, the thought of a bunch of Duskborn <i>doxxing </i>an elder into submission and then killing them and turning their remains into drugs. That's the crazy messed up stuff I like in my WoD</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Thiel#Early_career\" target=\"_blank\">Check it then</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-23-2022, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T07:38:11-08:00","id":1473072,"title":"","content":"I am now back! Had to delay for a month or two to do an Audible book deal.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T23:46:39-08:00","id":1473954,"title":"","content":"<b>The Bahari part 1</b><br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Cult<br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: A cult of feminist misandrists (no they aren't the same) who engage in a combination of better living through torture as well as gardening.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: Yeah, this was delayed by about four months, which goes to tell you that I was 1:] Distracted by a deal with Podium Entertainment. 2:] Writing no less than three books simultaneously (<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09Q1MS51G\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Space Academy Dropouts</i> </a>1 and 2, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09RMK3MQ1/\" target=\"_blank\">Daughter of the Cyber Dragons</a></i>). 3:] Struggling with the holidays. 4:] Dealing with a most unfortunate fact about the subject matter. 4:] is the one I have to confess to.<br /> <br /> I hate the Bahari.<br /> <br /> I feel embarrassed about saying it because it's a silly thing but I have hated the Lilith part of V:TM lore for over twenty five years. Seriously, I've hated it since <i>Revelations of the Dark Mother</i>. I was a huge fan of the <i>Book of Nod</i> and practically memorized it but I absolutely detested the writing in ROTDM. I didn't care for the Path of Lilith and I absolutely hated her followers every time they showed up in Noddist stories. I think my ultimate moment of dislike was reading the adventure &quot;Nightshade&quot; in the Gehenna supplement.<br /> <br /> That particular supplement had Lilith growing her garden of magic fruit, the PCs dealing with Lasombra and some other Antediluvians acting like Dick Dastardly, and the ending that they can either side with Lilith and dwell in wonder and glory forever in Paradise or be killed because they betrayed her. I feel like it was written by her publicist. I respect that she's Samael's wife in Kabbalah and has a &quot;legitimate&quot; role in demonology as well as folklore but it seems so damned weird.<br /> <br /> I can't even say what precisely irritates me so much about Lilith's use in the setting. I don't actually mind Lilith in the Verbena, where she makes even less sense, and my players like Lilith just fine (I use her regardless of my dislike). I think its that the Bahari seem so damned inconsistent and I'm not sure what their deal is. They like Gardens because, I guess the Garden of Eden even though vampires are divorced from the natural world. Pain because? I dunno. Pain is a thing Lilith causes? Its just hard.<br /> <br /> So I was admittedly delighted with the opening fiction here that included an extended, &quot;Just so you know, we're aware a lot of Lilith lore is a recent creation and not actually feminist.&quot; It also manages to make Lilith interesting in vampire for me because it casts her as an unknowable eldritch abomination that <i>her own followers</i> don't necessarily understand. It's honestly how I'd prefer they do Caine with the idea that he's something much-much older than Jewish myth but the Abrahamic types have used their own legends to try to explain it.<br /> <br /> I'm actually quite fond of this sort of thing and use it in my games a lot. The idea of a &quot;dark supernatural truth&quot; that religions and mythology are the interpretation of that isn't necessarily accurate gets used a lot when it's &quot;pagan&quot; myth but rarely for Abrahamic. It annoys me when that happens and it's partially why I once did a Call of Cthulhu scenario dealing with a cult that believed Yog-Sothoth was the God of Christianity and had a semi-decent argument. Maybe Caine is older than the original first murderer myth and his story got passed down to become the legend of Set and Osiris, Romulus and Remus, and Caine and Abel. Yes, there's some fratricide involved, probably, and some angelic beings but who knows what they are.<br /> <br /> Same for Lilith.<br /> <br /> Very cool idea, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-04-2022, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T13:18:32-08:00","id":1474052,"title":"","content":"I've not read this book, so I can't speak to how it depicts Lilith and the Bahari. I mostly liked the RotDM, but in the past the Bahari bored me. It seemed like, for lack of a better term, they were a bunch of one-note posers. That their ways of sticking it to the Man, and worshiping Lilith, just same down to some FemDom S&amp;M stuff and not much more. There are a lot of places an anti-Patricaral, bloody-minded group could go. But the Bahari seemed to go for the least interesting option.<br /> <br /> But they are hardly unique in that - lot of fan material is generated because official material is sometimes dull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T16:22:29-08:00","id":1474142,"title":"","content":"I like the general notions of having a matriarchal cult (or better: loosely related cults) of vampires centering around Lilith instead of Caine, even if through the filter of the Book of Nod. Hell, I would love to go full Circle of the Crone and have Eve (or Zilah), Lilith and the Crone as figures of worship or symbolism. Thing is... Bahari really feel badly developed, they feel like cringefest with the whole PAIN (gotta love it, gotta taste it, gotta do it) thing... like, I get the idea that Lilith suffered a ton of shit from basically everyone except maybe Satan, but to love pain like that seems just edgelordism. <br /> <br /> So in the end the values of Bahari are lost on me. They want what? Wisdom? Power? Be alone and develop freely? Grow as a community? Grow their magic gardens? Get Magic? Bring Lilith forth like the Setite's do with theirs? I really don't know, and if it is just 'hey, choose yourself gamemaster' then it is one of those cases that I feel like it was a badly developed thing, not something I can use freely and creatively. <br /> <br /> I believe they can be a fun idea, and a nice option, but till now (and maybe even now with Cults of Blood...) they have been empty and without direction. Most of the time they are really out of place, like Sabbat (wtf?), Camarilla (yeah... may... no, don't think so), Anarchs (yeah I suppose); but they should've been bigger, much bigger. They have a Book of Nod of their own in and out of universe, but I still get the Heresy of Caine and it's crazy gnosticism better than the Bahari. I really think they can be fun, and will work a bit on them with the Cults of the BLood Gods book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T16:54:49-08:00","id":1474144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1474142#post1474142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the general notions of having a matriarchal cult (or better: loosely related cults) of vampires centering around Lilith instead of Caine, even if through the filter of the Book of Nod. Hell, I would love to go full Circle of the Crone and have Eve (or Zilah), Lilith and the Crone as figures of worship or symbolism. Thing is... Bahari really feel badly developed, they feel like cringefest with the whole PAIN (gotta love it, gotta taste it, gotta do it) thing... like, I get the idea that Lilith suffered a ton of shit from basically everyone except maybe Satan, but to love pain like that seems just edgelordism.<br /> <br /> So in the end the values of Bahari are lost on me. They want what? Wisdom? Power? Be alone and develop freely? Grow as a community? Grow their magic gardens? Get Magic? Bring Lilith forth like the Setite's do with theirs? I really don't know, and if it is just 'hey, choose yourself gamemaster' then it is one of those cases that I feel like it was a badly developed thing, not something I can use freely and creatively.<br /> <br /> I believe they can be a fun idea, and a nice option, but till now (and maybe even now with Cults of Blood...) they have been empty and without direction. Most of the time they are really out of place, like Sabbat (wtf?), Camarilla (yeah... may... no, don't think so), Anarchs (yeah I suppose); but they should've been bigger, much bigger. They have a Book of Nod of their own in and out of universe, but I still get the Heresy of Caine and it's crazy gnosticism better than the Bahari. I really think they can be fun, and will work a bit on them with the Cults of the BLood Gods book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I feel like the Bahari would benefit if they actually leaned into what they always seem to attempt to shy away from: the idea of the cult being driven by feminine rage. The early Christian Church was driven in large part by its drive to convert slaves and women into their faith (getting a lot of traction due to the fact it forbid infanticide among other things).<br /> <br /> The idea of Lilith being a figure who specifically appeals to Kindred women with a chip on their shoulder from the misogyny of their home societies and Kindred men feels like it could be an excellent recruiting tool at the start. The cult of Lilith being a distinctly feminine vampire religion where the religion exalts in the fact that you're a blood-drinking, dominating, and ruthless monster designed to bring horror to mortals as well as non-Lilins.<br /> <br /> I mean, go big or go home. Why not have the Path of Lilith be something that tells you, &quot;Lilith was awful, be like Lilith!&quot;<br /> <br /> Certainly, I can think of plenty of people who vampires who'd be attracted to that kind of philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T16:55:50-08:00","id":1474145,"title":"","content":"The Bahari appeal to those who relate to Lilith. Those who have endured suffering, grief, loss, betrayal <i>et cetera</i> see Lilith as an example of what to be. She was betrayed, lost everything and yet she endured. To be a Bahari is to emulate Lilith, and draw strength from her, alleged, life. They seek to right where Lilith (and themselves) have been wronged, usually with violence. <br /> <br /> It is inaccurate to say they love pain. Pain to the Bahari is a way to make themselves feel closer to Lilith, to avoid letting themselves get comfortable. Lilith suffered and by suffering themselves they draw closer to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T17:31:22-08:00","id":1474147,"title":"","content":"Making it driven by &quot;Feminine Rage&quot; is limiting and simplistic. The Bahari already appeal to many issues commonly suffered by women, be it abuse, grief, or the inability to right when you have been wronged, and offer in turn acceptance, community and support in enacting justice, (or vengeance). And in it they also celebrate Lilith's femininity, her role as a grieving mother and a nurturer of a destroyed garden<br /> <br /> You'd be giving up the nuance on them, for another cheap man-hating women group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T19:20:32-08:00","id":1474156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1474147#post1474147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making it driven by &quot;Feminine Rage&quot; is limiting and simplistic. The Bahari already appeal to many issues commonly suffered by women, be it abuse, grief, or the inability to right when you have been wronged, and offer in turn acceptance, community and support in enacting justice, (or vengeance). And in it they also celebrate Lilith's femininity, her role as a grieving mother and a nurturer of a destroyed garden<br /> <br /> You'd be giving up the nuance on them, for another cheap man-hating women group.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume that appealing to feminine rage is something that is inherently uninteresting or invalid. Hatred of men is also not something that does not accompany hatred of misogyny. Certainly, the idea that women shouldn't be angry at their treatment is a erroneous idea and there are many masculine cults driven by ideas of rage as well as injustice. Wonder Woman is a figure that frequently is driven by feminine rage against injustices. So is Red Sonja. Both of which are my all time favorite comic book characters.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is that &quot;pain and grief are things suffered by Lilith so we revere that&quot; is that it's not actually an ideology. All of the cults are driven by suffering and horror because as a vampire you're a horribly cursed and tortured being. They don't do anything INTERESTING with it is the problem.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra do. The Lasombra deliberately infllict horrifying and nightmarish suffering on their subjects in order to make them stronger. Yet the Lasombra don't seem attracted to Lilith.<br /> <br /> What makes her cult special? I feel highlighting feminine issues in a cult makes it more interesting and deeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T21:49:08-08:00","id":1474160,"title":"","content":"I'll start this by addressing this, which I forgot to do so in my previous post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1474144#post1474144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea of Lilith being a figure who specifically appeals to Kindred women with a chip on their shoulder from the misogyny of their home societies and Kindred men feels like it could be an excellent recruiting tool at the start. The cult of Lilith being a distinctly feminine vampire religion where the religion exalts in the fact that you're a blood-drinking, dominating, and ruthless monster designed to bring horror to mortals as well as non-Lilins.<br /> <br /> I mean, go big or go home. Why not have the Path of Lilith be something that tells you, &quot;Lilith was awful, be like Lilith!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So Sabbat - Girls' Version? I feel its a bit redundant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You assume that appealing to feminine rage is something that is inherently uninteresting or invalid. Hatred of men is also not something that does not accompany hatred of misogyny. Certainly, the idea that women shouldn't be angry at their treatment is a erroneous idea and there are many masculine cults driven by ideas of rage as well as injustice. Wonder Woman is a figure that frequently is driven by feminine rage against injustices. So is Red Sonja. Both of which are my all time favorite comic book characters. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Appealing to feminine rage&quot; is uninteresting and invalid when you consider the cult already <b><i>does </i></b>that and more.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bahari are often sought out among survivors of abuse, crime, and events involving substantial fatalities (natural disasters, bus crashes, and the like). Mortals going through intense periods of grief (someone who may have lost all immediate family within a brief span of time, survivors of war)&quot;<br /> &quot;...Bahari still seek out those with broken hearts and broken will, but they also seek out those who have been deprived justice, as Lilith was... the rage and pain of a child taken from them in antiquity, or the husband lost to the hardships of life in a company town...&quot;<br /> <br /> What do you think this &quot;feminine rage&quot; you talk about is? Surviving abuse and injustices is already the core of the Bahari. The Bahari are those women who were abused, but they are also more than that. They are the woman who was betrayed by her allies, the father who lost his family, the vampire who was exiled from the court for something he didn't do.<br /> <br /> Obviously they are against misogyny, as the cult is inherently feminine and gendered issues are at the core of Lilith's story. But they are more than that. They aren't Feminism by Night, they are a group of people who relate to the story of a mythical being because it gives them meaning. They are also a cult of abuse-survivors who have turned to abusing others, and mutually enabling themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the issue is that &quot;pain and grief are things suffered by Lilith so we revere that&quot; is that it's not actually an ideology. All of the cults are driven by suffering and horror because as a vampire you're a horribly cursed and tortured being. They don't do anything INTERESTING with it is the problem. </div> </div> </div>You give far too much focus to the pain part, far more than it is given in it's V5 incarnation, which is the subject matter of this thread. But yes, they revere it because it is how they deal with it, as the cult draws numbers from abuse-survivors and the grieving. It is what Lilith suffered, and what they are indoctrinated to believe they need to suffer as well, as remember it <i>is a cult</i>, not a survivors group or a feminist organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra do. The Lasombra deliberately infllict horrifying and nightmarish suffering on their subjects in order to make them stronger. Yet the Lasombra don't seem attracted to Lilith. </div> </div> </div>Closest I've read to that is the Path of Night, and I don't see how it concerned with making their subject stronger as opposed to pure sadism. And I'm not the one who writes the books, assuming your previous sentence is accurate, the Lasombra should be attracted to the Bahari.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What makes her cult special? I feel highlighting feminine issues in a cult makes it more interesting and deeper. </div> </div> </div>Do tell what &quot;feminine issues&quot; you feel aren't already highlighted. <br /> <br /> Bottom line is, making the Bahari focused just on feminine issues is a gross simplification. You take the one major cult focused on a woman, and narrow it down to just feminine issues, because men can have diversity in their cults, women have womanly cults just for them. Because as I said before, the Bahari already deal in many subjects that are inherently close to many issues faced by women. Focusing on that would come at the cost of the other themes handled by the cult.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:03:01-08:00","id":1474195,"title":"","content":"<b>Pain</b><br /> I think that <i>Cults</i>' Bahari does use pain differently to older versions. They kind of believe that pain is a teacher, but it's more directed toward enemies and newbies, which sometimes means anybody but themselves and those Bahari above them in the pecking order. The enemies are often sacrificed anyway and the newbies are being hazed and maybe short-listed. Perhaps the Bahari teach each other to take <i>pride </i>in their trauma and don't really respect somebody until they've suffered like them.<br /> <br /> <b>Gardens</b><br /> I see some logic in the Gardens based on role in and following the story of creation. God made the Garden of Eden and assigned Adam as its steward; where's the Garden of Eden now? They failed. Lilith, having already been kicked out, made her own. Then Adam's son came along and ruined it. Then there's the world we have (or rather the World of Darkness). Some people like it, but Bahari don't because they recruit those that have especially suffered in it. So they try make utopias according their understanding of Lilith's ideas of utopias, although the Garden of Suffering might be more like a perfect Hell. Alternatively, they want to destroy the world so that Lilith is free to remake it in her design.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b><br /> Lasombra haven't been noted as a particularly common clan among the Bahari but what clan has? Still, a simplified reason that I suggest is that Lasombra are winners and Bahari are losers. Bahari have been beaten by a world that was probably rigged against them, traditionally by patriarchy, and so they reject it and want to make a new one. Lasombra keep playing. They don't hate the game, because they think they can still win and get what they want by conquering it. Besides, their suffering was typically the result of an individual Lasombra who believed that they had the potential to become like them. And for those Lasombra who do despair, there's also the Cult of Shalim, to which they have a more innate affinity. For all that, the last Bahari narrators in <i>Anarch </i>was a Lasombra called Nezha; she ends her piece with a characteristically Darwinian note. Also, there's probably something thematic that could be done with Lasombra and aquatic Bahari.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat</b><br /> It's funny that SetiteFriend described CTPhipps idea as &quot;Sabbat - Girls' Version&quot; because from what I've seen of the new Sabbat guide preview, it brings Bahari closer to the Sabbat's mainstream, with a path of enlightment and some doctrine that somehow reconciles them with Cainites. I hope to read how that's received here in future.<br /> <br /> <b>Midsommar</b><br /> There must be better sources of inspiration, but I think this film shares some themes.<ul><li>Dani's sister kill herself and their parents. That's remarkable bereavement.</li> <li>Dani is scorned by a man. Or so she and quite a lot of viewers are led to believe.</li> <li>The cult acknowledges Dani's pain, if in a rather crude way that doesn't show empathy, Pelle aside.</li> <li>Dani joins the community and their most brutal rites. I don't really understand why, but it involved grief, love bombing and drugs, which is just one point where my comparison to the Bahari falls apart. I suppose they <i>could</i> use love bombing and drugs.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T06:53:16-08:00","id":1475774,"title":"","content":"<b>The Bahari part 2</b><br /> <br /> <b>Synopsis</b>: The Bahari and their goals as well as methodology.<br /> <br /> <b>Analysis</b>: I feel absolutely terrible about this because I just don't feel like I'm very good at articulating anything new to the Bahari. I've been trying to come up with a great set of posts for the past month but I just am blanking on it. So, forgive me if this is not going to be a very long entry on the subject compared to the other cults. The next part of the cult's entries give us an explanation of the way the Bahari religion believes and the various Gardens that play roles in her religion. I actually really like this section because the Bahari are portrayed as a group that is absolutely a <i>mess</i> of contradictions and that their shared mythology gives them less in common than you might think.<br /> <br /> One thing Lilith worshipers have going for them, you see, is they are an OLD Kindred religion. Like the Church of Caine, they are thousands and possibly tens of thousands of years old. This makes it a marked contrast to many other religions found in this book and even modern religions. About the only thing you might find equally old among Kindred would be the worship of Haqim.<br /> <br /> The big thing this means is that the Bahari have sects, disputed texts, disputed ideologies, and variations on a theme. Some of them have &quot;avenging angels against abusive men&quot;, some are literal ****ing baby eaters (we'll get to that later), some are people who are obsessive environmentalists like werewolves, and others are S&amp;M Cenobites that would make Clive Barker proud. Presumably those are Tzimisce Bahari.<br /> <br /> I do actually note the book is pretty clear that the Lilin are a group that is pretty awful even by vampire standards and it needs to spell out they aren't the good guys. I don't recall any other cultist getting those kind of caveats. The book sort of assumes you know that vampires are bad but this one feels the need to <i>point it out</i>. There's whole sections on the Bahari being hypocrites who don't rescue enslaved women, go after men for no reason other than their sex, and are deeply hypocritical in their avenging angle business.<br /> <br /> Then there's the baby-eating. I actually liked this because they went there. The Bahari don't do that anymore. Honest. Okay, SOME of them do it but the majority of them know this is the kind of thing that attracts unwanted mortal attention and pisses off even Humanity 4-5 vampires at times. However, the SOME do really insist infant blood is delicious. Because it is. Like tasty human veal. I assume this is practiced either by Lilith worshiping fundamentalists who really insist, 100%, you can't get rid of the fact Lilith menaces children and pregnant woman because you don't pick and choose your parts of the Revelations of the Dark Mother OR it's done by people who signed up to the Bahari to be complete assholes.<br /> <br /> The Bahari have apparently taken over Budapesh (which I learned how to pronounce from The Black Widow), with an overwhelming 60% of their number being Bahari. This sounds impressive but they have a population of 1.7 million so that's actually about nine or ten vampires in the city. Well, depending on how you interpret the 1:100K line. In my games, I tend to say that vampires are so overpopulated that it's usually at least 200% of that number.<br /> <br /> Some rituals too but I don't really jive with Thaumaturgy/Blood Sorcery that much so not much to say here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-04-2022, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T08:18:26-08:00","id":1475775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475774#post1475774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[The Bahari have apparently taken over Budapesh (which I learned how to pronounce from The Black Widow), with an overwhelming 60% of their number being Bahari. This sounds impressive but they have a population of 1.7 million so that's actually about nine or ten vampires in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember giggling when I read that and thought, &quot;Oh gee, you mean there's a whole half-dozen Bahari there? How very impressive.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T10:58:44-08:00","id":1475784,"title":"","content":"That ratio has always been stupid tbh, not to mention usually ignored by the actual books.1 vampire per 10,000, as presented in V5, is much more sensible. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T12:02:35-08:00","id":1475791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475784#post1475784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That ratio has always been stupid tbh, not to mention usually ignored by the actual books.1 vampire per 10,000, as presented in V5, is much more sensible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That seems pretty ridiculous that no one has noticed the supernatural though, especially if you assume other supernaturals are real. That would mean we have a couple of vampires even in the middle of my nowhere town.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T09:31:36-08:00","id":1475842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475791#post1475791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems pretty ridiculous that no one has noticed the supernatural though, especially if you assume other supernaturals are real. That would mean we have a couple of vampires even in the middle of my nowhere town.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a lot easier to go unnoticed when you\u2019re not regularly leaving bodies around from feeding, being fed on feels really good, and the people doing the feeding have mind-control powers, lots of money and influence to cover it up.<br /> <br /> 1-in-10,000 means that, even taking 3BP/night on average, it would take 9 years to feed from each one once (at 1 BP per victim). This isn\u2019t counting willing blood dolls who get off on the high of the Kiss and come back for more as often as they can.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the US mortality from all causes is about 80-90 per 10k per year in the real world (and the WoD is supposedly more violent). Even at 1:10k every vampire in a city would have to be leaving a body practically every month before their feeding starts going above the level of statistical noise, particularly in high violent crime areas where the mortality rate is higher than the nationwide average.<br /> <br /> Also worth remembering is that there\u2019s an actual psychological limit on how many people you can actually keep track of as individuals of about 150. The odds of even a dozen deaths a year even being noticed by any more than 1800 of any given group of 10,000 is pretty slim, and that\u2019s acquaintance-level relationships (i.e. your regular waitress at the diner isn\u2019t serving you anymore\u2026 if you actually ask about them (and don\u2019t just presume they got a better job somewhere) and find out they died in some accident you\u2019ll feel a little bad, but it\u2019s not going to ping as \u201cvampire predation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Basically, 1:100k is so safe as to be boring. Draining a victim dry once a week wouldn\u2019t even push the mortality rate outside of statistical norms. 1:10k is still pretty safe, but importantly for this being an RPG, presents at least some risks of being discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 03-05-2022, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T15:14:13-08:00","id":1476288,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FNqM2EeWUAIlxw-?format=jpg&amp;name=small\" target=\"_blank\">Relevant to the Bahari...</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T19:10:35-08:00","id":1476303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475842#post1475842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a lot easier to go unnoticed when you\u2019re not regularly leaving bodies around from feeding, being fed on feels really good, and the people doing the feeding have mind-control powers, lots of money and influence to cover it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is a lot easier. Yet in a society you can't expect everyone to play along acting in the safest and most sensible manner. You need room for accidents and general idiocy. It's hard to have half a dozen people not mess up with anything IRL, you expect Vampires in the World of Darkness to behave?<br /> <br /> Mind-control powers, money and influence also do a lot, indeed, but not once you push things too far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475842#post1475842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-in-10,000 means that, even taking 3BP/night on average, it would take 9 years to feed from each one once (at 1 BP per victim).</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can guarantee a near perfect spread where you somehow manage to feed on virtually everyone at least once, sure, you're only making the area have a weird symptom that everyone feel once a decade. But in all likelihood you can't spread your feedings that way, you have feeding grounds, hours and tactics that in practice greatly reduce your actual pool of victims, which means more exposition in consistent circumstances and with consistent victims to make some noise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475842#post1475842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn\u2019t counting willing blood dolls who get off on the high of the Kiss and come back for more as often as they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is 1 BP/month tops with a heavy iron-based diet if you want them to live long. It helps, but isn't really feasible as a staple for your diet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475842#post1475842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, the US mortality from all causes is about 80-90 per 10k per year</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem being that this is precisely &quot;mortality from all causes&quot;. Even in the most violent places in the world the great majority of deaths isn't violence-related or unknown causes. In fact, even accidents aren't that a common cause of death. <a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/fastats/deaths.htm\" target=\"_blank\">According to the CDC</a>, the leading causes of death in 2020 in the US were the same as everywhere else: heart diseases and cancer, together they were 38.4% of all deaths and those are deaths that are usually very well documented.<br /> <br /> Covid-19 was the next, being the reason for the average peaking at more than 100 per 10k that year, if we remove those 350k deaths from the equation to correct pandemic noise in our statistic, the previous diseases are 42.84% of the &quot;expected&quot; deaths. The next <b>seven</b> main causes of death in the US in 2020 are, in this order, accidents, stroke, chronic lower respiratory diseases, Alzheimer's, diabetes, influenza + pneumonia and kidney diseases.<br /> <br /> For an interesting comparison, Covid-19 was found through investigation of just 40 excess cases of antibiotic-resistant pneumonia. 40, not deaths, just pneumonia, <b>in a metropolis of more than 12 million inhabitants</b>. How many people get sick there every day? And still on comparisons, a statistic on <a href=\"https://www.healthdata.org/brazil-rio-de-janeiro\" target=\"_blank\">death rates in Rio de Janeiro</a>, recognized as very violent, comparing 2009 and 2019, shows violence as the... 4th cause back in 2009, falling to 5th now, of course there's no Covid-19 and in general the results are quite similar. Feira de Santana, the actual most violent city in Brazil, has a <b>murder</b> rate below 7 per 10k...<br /> <br /> So the statistical noise depends a lot on circumstances, comparing with the combined deaths by every cause isn't in any way what would happen. To determine if it is above statistical noise you must first determine the <b><i>relevant</i></b> statistical background, the deaths that actually bear any similarity to what a vampire leaves behind. If you get murders and disappearances, then you'll have far lower numbers to run with and hide bodies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475842#post1475842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth remembering is that there\u2019s an actual psychological limit on how many people you can actually keep track of as individuals of about 150.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that's a legend. Second, even in the legend it doesn't work like that, third it is irrelevant. Noticing things through personal experience is a character's background, not a measure of a society finding out something. People will notice excessive deaths because there are a lot of people who <b>jobs</b> include dealing with this. If vampire attacks cause an increase in hospitalization, hospital workers will notice because they <b>work in the hospital</b>, not because more people they know are being hospitalized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460766-wir-cults-of-the-blood-gods?p=1475842#post1475842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, 1:100k is so safe as to be boring. Draining a victim dry once a week wouldn\u2019t even push the mortality rate outside of statistical norms. 1:10k is still pretty safe, but importantly for this being an RPG, presents at least some risks of being discovered.</div> </div> </div> </div>1:10k is feasible, not safe. At least not under V:tM premises. The problem is precisely that a city with 1:10k Kindred is under pressure for population reasons alone, creating actual risk for the Kindred from the mortal population and with population control at its peak.<br /> <br /> That's an interesting proposition for a game, a very valid one, but far from a good default as 1:50-100k simply lets you ignore such things and focus your game elsewhere. I do agree that the proportion in a city may be greater than 1:100k, maybe 1:50k or even 1:30k, although with some considerations.<br /> <br /> But 1:10k is safe only under the most simplistic view of the question, ignoring anything about what a city is beyond a number of inhabitants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}